window.AKK_MISTAKEN_SYSTEM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_MISTAKEN_SYSTEM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: The System","paragraphs":["“Ah, finally, time to clock out.”","Jiang Yanyan stretched deeply. She pressed the final checkout button on the supermarket’s register, carefully counted the day’s earnings, and put the money away.","The supermarket in front of her was the entire foundation of her life.","It was a two-and-a-half-story, five-bay building that she had built herself, with red brick walls and white plaster. Sturdy and imposing, it had an air of quiet prosperity.","The entire first floor consisted of five storefronts that she had knocked together and converted into a supermarket. From rice, flour, cooking oil, and salt to snacks and drinks, from daily necessities to small hardware items, the shelves were packed to the brim. It was the neighborhood’s most dependable convenience store.","Behind the supermarket was a spacious courtyard paved with bluestone. There was a side room on either side, and farther back stood an enormous storage shed.","It was usually filled with the supermarket’s backup supplies—rice, flour, oil, toilet paper, laundry detergent, and other consumables. The shed was large enough to ensure that the supermarket would never run out of stock.","The second floor and the half-story attic were Jiang Yanyan’s private space. They contained a bedroom, living room, walk-in closet, and small study, all furnished to create a warm and comfortable home.","From the second-floor balcony, she could look down at the greenery in the courtyard. Beyond it lay her three mu of private farmland, a shimmering fishpond, and, behind the pond, a range of rolling hills.","This was the property her parents had left her. They had passed away when she was young, and rather than go to a big city to struggle, she stayed behind to look after the building, the supermarket, the fields, and the fishpond, living a leisurely, unhurried life.","During the day, she watched the store. Whenever customers came in, she greeted them warmly; when there was no one around, she curled up on the little chair behind the register to watch dramas or read novels. When she got hungry, she picked some vegetables from the courtyard, caught a fish from the pond, and cooked herself a simple meal.","Whenever she had free time, she went to the three mu of farmland to plant vegetables and water them, fed the fish in the pond, wandered through the hills behind the house, planted a few fruit trees, and raised some chickens and ducks.","There was no scheming in the workplace and none of the noisy pressure of the big city. Her days were simple and comfortable. Jiang Yanyan had long since grown accustomed to this life, and she genuinely loved its stability.","Business had been a little better than usual today, and she hadn’t finally gotten a break until after nine in the evening.","Jiang Yanyan pulled down and locked the supermarket’s rolling shutters one by one. She straightened the disorderly goods on the shelves, wiped down the register and the floor, then picked up her small bag and climbed the stairs to the second floor.","After washing up, she changed into soft cotton pajamas and sprawled across the bed. She casually picked up her phone and opened a modern wealthy-family novel she had started a few days earlier but hadn’t finished.","The female supporting character in the novel was named Zhang Yanyan. She was the heiress of Zhang Group, one of Rong City’s four great families. Reserved and low-key, she excelled academically, yet she had fallen in love with the male lead, Song Ze, despite his ordinary family background.","In the end, she was murdered by the male lead and the innocent-looking female lead, Tang Tang, working together. Her parents spent their twilight years in misery, while the male lead and the female lead rode on the power of the Tang family and lived prosperous, successful lives.","Jiang Yanyan grew increasingly annoyed as she read. She muttered a few complaints about the scumbag male lead and the fake-sweet female lead, calling the female supporting character hopelessly love-struck. Then sleepiness overcame her. She tossed her phone onto the bedside table, pulled the covers over her head, and fell asleep.","She never could have imagined that when she woke up, the world would have been turned upside down.","In a haze of semi-consciousness, Jiang Yanyan felt a buzzing in her head, as though countless tiny needles were gently pricking her. Then, a cold, emotionless mechanical voice suddenly exploded deep within her mind:","[Suitable soul detected. Sign-in System 0018 is binding...]","[Binding successful! Hello, host Zhang Yanyan. I am Sign-in System 0018.]","[Transferring to the designated small world... Transfer successful!]","After a string of notification sounds, Jiang Yanyan abruptly opened her eyes.","Instead of the familiar bedroom with its warm wallpaper, she saw an ornate crystal chandelier overhead. The ceiling was high and decorated in an elaborate European style. Beneath her was a soft velvet bed that seemed to swallow her whole, and she was covered by smooth, luxurious silk sheets.","She sat up and looked around.","This bedroom was absurdly large and extravagantly furnished. There was a European-style wardrobe with carved details, a full-length dressing mirror, and an elegant bay window layered with a plush carpet. In one corner stood a leather sofa and a small tea table. Every object exuded the unmistakable scent of money.","An unfamiliar room. Unfamiliar furnishings. Everything was unfamiliar.","Jiang Yanyan’s heart sank. She instinctively reached toward the bedside table, but her phone and familiar pillow were nowhere to be found. Even the scent in the air was different—a faint fragrance from an aromatherapy diffuser instead of the clean smell of her usual laundry detergent.","“Who is that? Who was speaking just now?” Jiang Yanyan suppressed the panic rising in her heart and spoke in a low voice. Her tone was slightly hoarse from sleep, but it still carried an unmistakable calmness.","She had lived for twenty-five years. She might not have been good at many things, but she had developed the ability to remain calm in a crisis. Even when faced with an unfamiliar situation, she would not lose her head.","[Host, I am Sign-in System 0018. I am inside your consciousness.]","The mechanical voice sounded again, clearer this time, though its tone remained cold and emotionless. [I have successfully bonded with you. From now on, I will take you through various small worlds to complete sign-in missions.]","Jiang Yanyan frowned. “Travel between worlds? I was sleeping at home. Why would I suddenly travel somewhere? And when did I ever agree to let you bind with me?”","[Zzzt... That’s right, Zhang Yanyan.]","[Our scan detected that your soul has a 100% compatibility rate with the original host of this small world, so you were transferred here to take over the original host’s life.]","“What? Zhang Yanyan? That’s the youngest daughter of the Zhang family, my neighbor from back home. Did you get the wrong person? My name is Jiang Yanyan!”","[Jiang Yanyan?]","A sharp burst of static suddenly tore through the air. System 0018’s mechanical voice immediately fell out of rhythm, its panic unmistakable.","[Unknown error detected... Data comparison failed... Binding target mismatch!]","After a pause of two seconds, the system’s voice finally lost its initial icy detachment and became somewhat awkward and flustered.","[Apologies, host. I made an error during verification. The target souls had similar names and overlapping locations, so I mistakenly bound myself to the wrong person.]","Jiang Yanyan’s heart gave a sudden jolt. She immediately thought of the novel she had been reading before bed.","“So where exactly have you sent me?”","System 0018’s voice dropped half an octave, losing some of its mechanical quality and gaining a hint of guilt. 【The original host, Zhang Yanyan, is the heiress of Zhang Group. The current story point is the end of the gaokao. In one week, you’ll enroll at Tengyuan University, where you’ll give a speech as the freshman representative. That will also be the first time you meet the male lead, Song Ze.】","Jiang Yanyan was so furious that she nearly laughed.","She had been perfectly happy running her supermarket and living a quiet, stable life. Yet after going to sleep, she had been forcibly bound to this ridiculous system and tossed into a novel to play a cannon-fodder female supporting character?","What kind of international joke was this?","“I refuse,” Jiang Yanyan said without the slightest hesitation. “I want to go back—to my own world, my supermarket, my courtyard, my fields, my fishponds... I don’t want to stay in this lousy little world.”","【I’m sorry, Host. Once the binding takes effect, it cannot be undone. After transmission is complete, you cannot return to your original world.】 System 0018’s tone grew more urgent. 【Please accept reality and settle into your life in this small world. All you need to do is complete the daily check-in.】","“Can’t return? Can’t undo the binding?”","Jiang Yanyan’s voice lowered, and a dark glint flashed through her eyes. “You forcibly bound my soul without my consent and dragged me here from my original world. And now you’re telling me I can’t go back? Do you realize that this is an illegal binding? I’m filing a complaint with your administration department right now.”","Although she was only an ordinary supermarket owner, she knew a thing or two about reason and fairness. This system was clearly taking advantage of its abilities to manipulate the soul of an ordinary person. It was completely outrageous.","The moment it heard the word “complaint,” System 0018 panicked completely. Static crackled, and its voice was filled with urgency. 【Don’t! Host, you absolutely mustn’t! Once a complaint is submitted, I’ll be recalled and reset immediately. I won’t even be able to preserve my core data!】","“I couldn’t care less whether you get reset.” Jiang Yanyan raised an eyebrow, her tone utterly indifferent. “Either send me back to my original world, or we can both go down together. You choose.”","She had calculated that the system couldn’t possibly give up on its bond with her, nor did it want to meet the fate of being destroyed. After all, a system’s very purpose was to bind itself to a host and carry out missions. If the matter reached the administration department, it would never come out ahead.","System 0018 fell silent for a full three or four seconds. The urgency in its mechanical voice gradually faded, replaced by helplessness. 【It was my work error, and I caused you losses. Within the limits of my authority, I can offer you appropriate compensation.】","“Of course it was your error,” Jiang Yanyan replied. “The person you were supposed to bind wasn’t me in the first place.”"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Yunhua Space","paragraphs":["The anger burning in her heart only grew hotter. So she was the unlucky one here—because of a mistake made by the system, she had been forced to leave her home, abandon everything, and come to this unfamiliar place to play the role of cannon fodder.","Returning was already impossible. The system had made it clear that there was no way back, so all she could do was settle for the next best thing and fight for the greatest benefits possible.","Everything she had was in her original world: Yunhua Supermarket, the self-built house, the courtyard, the storage shed, the rooms on either side of the house, the three acres of land, the fishpond, and the mountain behind it. That was her home—the place she cared about most.","Since she couldn’t go back, she would bring all of it with her.","“Don’t give me any of that useless nonsense.” Jiang Yanyan spoke slowly and clearly. “I want my original five-bay, two-and-a-half-story self-built house, the Yunhua Supermarket on the first floor, the courtyard behind it, the storage shed, the rooms on both sides, the three acres of land behind the house, the fishpond beside it, and the mountain behind the fishpond—all of it transformed into my private space. Only I can enter it, and I have complete control over it.”","She stated her demands clearly and waited for the system’s response.","System 0018 fell silent once more. It was obvious that the system’s backend was rapidly calculating the required permissions. After a long pause, it finally spoke hesitantly:","【A self-built house, supermarket, courtyard, farmland, and other properties... That’s a considerable area. I need to access the highest-level permissions...】","“If you can’t do it, forget it. I’ll file a complaint right now.” Jiang Yanyan made her threat without hesitation.","【Wait, wait! I agree!】 System 0018 immediately backed down. 【It can be converted into a private space bound to your soul. Only you will be able to enter it, and you will have complete control over it. It will follow you through every small world. That much is within my authority to decide.】","Jiang Yanyan breathed a sigh of relief. Now that was more like it.","But she didn’t rush to finalize the deal. Instead, she immediately pressed the key issue. “How exactly will this space operate? There have to be rules. Tell me the complete operating rules first. And what about the system’s check-in function?”","System 0018’s orderly electronic voice rang out:","【The basic operating rules of the space are as follows:","1. Supplies taken from the supermarket inside the space will automatically be restocked the following day. As long as there is sufficient energy, the supplies will never run out.","2. Time inside the space flows at ten times the speed of the outside world. Crops, livestock, poultry, and fish grow at ten times the outside rate. This will have no effect on the host’s body.","3. Jade is the space’s only source of energy. Once placed inside, it will automatically be converted into power to support all the space’s functions.","4. The system may be checked in once a day. Daily rewards consist of ordinary items. Special rewards will be issued during holidays and festivals. Reward grades are divided into white, green, blue, purple, orange, red, and multicolored, with multicolored being the highest grade.","5. The space is soul-bound to the host and cannot be separated from her. Others will be unable to detect it or enter it.】","After hearing the rules, Jiang Yanyan immediately identified the key to the space’s operation and took the opportunity to demand additional compensation.","“Since your mistake in binding me caused all of this, simply giving me the space isn’t enough. First, add a spiritual spring to the space—one that can improve my health, purge impurities from my body, and neutralize all poisons. Consider it extra compensation for your mistake.”","System 0018 paused, as though the request caused it considerable pain, but it still agreed:","【...Fine. I’ll give you an exclusive spiritual spring with the effects you described.】","“Second, the rules say the space needs jade as an energy source to operate. I’ve just transmigrated here with nothing to my name, so you need to give me an initial stockpile of jade—enough to keep the space running in its early stages. The more, the better.” Jiang Yanyan refused to yield an inch.","[ Jade is the core energy source of the space. I’ll immediately transfer all the jade jewelry from the walk-in closet on the second floor of your original home to beside the spiritual spring in the space. I’ll also provide an additional batch of high-quality natural jade as startup energy for the space. ]","Afraid that Jiang Yanyan would continue pressing the matter, System 0018 hurriedly added, [ The more jade you collect in the future, the more energy the space will have. Not only will it unlock hidden surprise features, but it can also level up. The land, fishpond, and forest will all expand dramatically!","What’s more, any spatial treasures you obtain in other small worlds in the future can be completely merged with this space, becoming yours alone to control. ]","Jiang Yanyan’s heart leapt with delight. This added benefit far exceeded her expectations, and she finally nodded in satisfaction. “Now that’s more like it.”","[ Activating space... Activation successful! ]","[ The space has been soul-bound to the host. The host may enter and leave freely. ]","[ Please name the space. ]","Without a moment’s hesitation, Jiang Yanyan blurted out, “Yunhua.”","That was the name of her supermarket—the thing she missed most. Now that the space was called Yunhua, it was as though she had brought her home along with her.","[ Space successfully named: Yunhua Space. ]","Having settled the most important matter—the space—Jiang Yanyan remembered another crucial question. “What missions do I need to complete after transmigrating into this small world? Are there any mandatory requirements? Will I be punished if I fail them?”","She had no desire to be forced around by a system. Her goal was to tend fields, stockpile supplies, and live a peaceful life with Yunhua Space. She certainly did not want to be bound by missions.","[ Don’t worry. I’m a laid-back sign-in system. There are no mandatory missions, nor are there any punishments. ] System 0018’s tone became relaxed again. [ You only need to protect the original owner and her family, and make sure they don’t meet a tragic end. Beyond that, you can do whatever you want. Even if you simply idle your days away, I won’t interfere in the slightest. ]","Jiang Yanyan was completely reassured.","No mandatory missions, no punishments—she only had to change the fate of the original owner and her parents. For the rest of her time, she could farm, hoard supplies, and enjoy a peaceful retirement in Yunhua Space. Perfect!","Then she came back to her senses and looked at the system. “Now that I’m inhabiting the original owner’s body, how do I obtain her memories? Without them, I won’t understand anything about this place.”","[ The host only needs to confirm with a thought, and I can transmit all of the original owner’s memories intact into your mind. The process will be completely painless, ] System 0018 explained patiently before asking, [ Host, are you ready to receive the original owner’s memories? ]","“I’m ready. Start the transfer.” Jiang Yanyan took a deep breath.","[ Original owner’s memory transfer in progress... 10%... 50%... 100%. Transfer complete! ]","A vast flood of fragmented memories surged into Jiang Yanyan’s mind like a tidal wave. Once she had processed all the information, she suddenly realized that she had transmigrated into a wealthy-family novel she had read just a few days ago!","The original owner of the body was named Zhang Yanyan. Eighteen years old, she had just finished the college entrance examinations and been admitted to Tengyuan University, Rongcheng’s most prestigious private university, with outstanding grades. She had even been chosen as the freshman representative and was due to give a speech at the opening ceremony.","The Zhang family was one of Rongcheng’s Four Great Families. The Zhang Group had holdings in real estate, technology, retail, and numerous other sectors. With assets worth hundreds of billions, they were among Rongcheng’s most elite and powerful families.","Zhang Yanyan’s parents, Zhang Zhenbang and Su Wan, were usually too busy with work to spend much time with her. Even so, they doted on her immensely and granted her every wish.","Zhang Yanyan was quiet and reserved by nature, never one to draw attention to herself. She never mentioned her family background in front of others. At school, she had always been known simply as a top student, and everyone assumed she was just an exceptionally gifted girl from an ordinary family.","Tengyuan University was a prestigious private institution, and many of its students came from wealth and influence. Some were rich kids with poor grades who had enrolled merely to add polish to their credentials; others had earned their places through exceptional academic achievement.","Zhang Yanyan belonged to the rare group who possessed both a privileged background and outstanding grades. The male lead of the novel, Song Ze, belonged to the latter.","Song Ze came from an extremely impoverished family. To sum it up: a sick mother, a gambling father, an idle younger brother, and a broken version of himself. The entire burden of supporting the family rested on his mother alone.","He appeared refined and handsome, with excellent grades, but deep down he was both profoundly insecure and intensely greedy. All he wanted was to attach himself to the powerful and wealthy, forcing his way into high society."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: First Check-in","paragraphs":["At the opening ceremony, Song Ze saw the original host delivering a speech as the freshman representative. She was beautiful and excelled academically. Thinking she came from an ordinary family, Song Ze believed that dating her would make him look good when he brought her around, while her modest background would also make her easy to control. So he began pursuing her relentlessly.","Of course, the main reason was that the original host was the most suitable girl he could reach at the time.","He brought her breakfast every day, busied himself with everything for her, and showed her endless care and concern. After half a month of persistence, the original host—who had never been in love before—softened and agreed to date him.","The two spent a peaceful year together, until a girl named Tang Tang transferred into their class during their second year.","Tang Tang had the standard delicate, innocent appearance of a white lotus. Her mother had raised her by selling breakfast from a street stall, and Tang Tang, with her excellent grades, had been specially admitted to Tengyuan University. She looked weak and pitiful, but was actually very calculating.","She was the illegitimate daughter of Tang Limin, general manager of the Tang Group. Although the Tang Group belonged to a third-rate family in Rongcheng, it was still hundreds of times wealthier than an ordinary household.","Tang Tang had always concealed her identity, waiting for the chance to be acknowledged by her biological family.","After an unexpected incident revealed Tang Tang’s true identity to Song Ze, he immediately began plotting.","He felt that the original host’s ordinary family could offer him no help, whereas the Tang family behind Tang Tang could save him decades of hard work.","Thus, he began distancing himself from the original host while maintaining an ambiguous relationship with Tang Tang.","One day, the original host went shopping with her roommates. Song Ze and Tang Tang happened to be eating at the same restaurant. Their intimate behavior was witnessed by the original host.","Unable to contain her anger, she went over to confront Tang Tang. Song Ze, however, shielded Tang Tang and turned the accusation back on the original host, claiming that she was petty and suspicious, and that she was slandering him and Tang Tang by questioning their innocence. He then proposed breaking up with her on the spot.","The original host had never possessed very deep feelings for Song Ze. She simply could not stand the way he and Tang Tang acted shamelessly while pretending to be innocent. He had cheated on her and was now shifting the blame, and she could not swallow her resentment. Thus, she refused to accept the breakup and began opposing the two of them at every turn.","The entanglement among the three caused a huge uproar, and before long, half of Tengyuan University knew about it.","Not long afterward, Tang Tang deliberately sent the original host a message to provoke her, saying that she and Song Ze were on a date on the rooftop and that the original host should know her place and get lost.","Burning with rage, the original host rushed to the rooftop, where she caught Song Ze and Tang Tang confessing their feelings to each other and embracing. She immediately charged forward and began fighting Tang Tang.","Song Ze desperately protected Tang Tang. During the struggle, the original host was pushed off the rooftop and died on the spot.","Song Ze and Tang Tang were scared out of their wits. Taking advantage of the chaos, they fled the scene.","When the original host’s parents learned of their daughter’s death, they were devastated. They immediately flew back to the country and swore to make the culprit who had killed their daughter pay.","There had been no surveillance cameras on the rooftop, however, so there was no way to verify what had happened. Moreover, both Song Ze and Tang Tang insisted that it had merely been an accident.","In the end, the judicial authorities could only base their ruling on the circumstances at the scene. Song Ze and Tang Tang were each convicted of involuntary manslaughter and sentenced to several years in prison.","The elderly couple had lost their only daughter in such a tragic way, while the murderer had received only a few years in prison. Naturally, they were unwilling to accept it. Unfortunately, the other members of the Zhang family had also begun fighting fiercely over control of the family business, and by then, the couple’s health was already failing.","Before long, the two of them passed away one after the other.","Before their deaths, the couple could not bear to see the Zhang Group—which they had spent their entire lives building—fall into the hands of the Zhang clan, where the various relatives would scheme against one another and carve it up. After careful consideration, they entrusted all their property and the company’s shares to the daughter of their younger male cousin, a girl whose appearance closely resembled that of the original host.","The members of the Zhang clan had long coveted the family fortune. When they saw that the inheritance had already been settled and a successor chosen, they were deeply dissatisfied and often went looking for trouble.","Fortunately, none of them succeeded.","After serving their sentences, Song Ze and Tang Tang were released from prison one after another.","Their lives were not affected much after their release. With the Tang family’s resources supporting them, they continued to live carefree, prosperous lives.","According to the original plot, Tang Tang’s half-sister later developed kidney disease and needed a transplant. Tang Tang happened to be a suitable donor, so she used the opportunity as leverage, demanding to be acknowledged by the Tang family and claiming half of the shares under Tang Limin’s name.","Tang Limin’s wife was in poor health and had given birth to only one daughter. In order to save her child, she agreed to all of Tang Tang’s demands.","After donating a kidney, Tang Tang’s health deteriorated, but she successfully became a member of the Tang family.","After receiving the transplant, Tang Tang’s half-sister survived only a few more years before passing away.","After her daughter’s death, Tang Limin’s wife lost the will to go on. Her health had already been poor, and she soon died as well.","After Tang Limin passed away, Tang Tang and Song Ze inherited his shares. They collected enormous dividends every year, lived extraordinarily comfortable lives, and eventually enjoyed a peaceful old age.","After the original host died, her soul drifted through the world. Only then did she learn that she had been living inside a novel. She was the villainess, a character whose role was to advance the romance between the male and female leads—a stepping stone to their happy life.","She was filled with hatred.","She had never truly loved Song Ze. She had only accepted his pursuit out of momentary curiosity, yet she had been manipulated by the plot into entangling herself with the male and female leads like a fool. In the end, she had died tragically, bringing grief to her parents and leaving them to die with their family destroyed.","She was unwilling to accept such a fate, but she could not break free from the control of the plot. All she could do was give up her chance at reincarnation and pray that someone would enter her body, change this tragic destiny, prevent herself from being controlled by the plot, protect her parents, and stay far away from the scumbag and the scheming woman.","And Jiang Yanyan was the person who had been mistakenly bound by the system and brought into this world.","After receiving all the memories, Jiang Yanyan rubbed her aching temples. A chill flashed through her eyes.","Song Ze, Tang Tang, and the Tang family behind them—what a fine bunch they were.","The original host had been kind and innocent, yet she had been harmed by a scumbag and a scheming woman and died tragically on a rooftop. Her parents had lost their only daughter and died with resentment in their hearts, while the male and female leads had safely endured their prison sentences, continued to possess wealth, and lived out their lives in comfort.","But now, Jiang Yanyan had arrived.","She was not the original host. She would not be deceived by a scumbag’s honeyed words, nor would she pretend to get along with some innocent-looking schemer.","As for the love between Song Ze and Tang Tang, they could play out their romance by themselves. They had better not come anywhere near her. They could forget about dragging her into the role of a cannon fodder again just to highlight their so-called love and devotion.","Her goal was simple: protect the original host’s parents, safeguard the Zhang family’s fortune, stay away from every character connected to the plot, and devote herself to her Cloudflower Space—growing crops, stockpiling supplies, and living a good life.","That was all she wanted.","As for that scumbag and that scheming woman, she would leave them alone as long as they did not provoke her. But if they dared come looking for trouble, she would not mind letting them taste the consequences a little earlier.","After sorting through all her thoughts, Jiang Yanyan moved her mind, and in an instant, she vanished from the luxurious bedroom and entered the Cloudflower Space.","The next moment, a familiar scene appeared before her eyes.","A sturdy, self-built house with five bays and two and a half stories stood in the center of the space. The Cloudflower Supermarket on the first floor was brightly lit, and all the goods on its shelves were arranged neatly, exactly as they had been when she left.","The bluestone paving in the courtyard, the east and west side rooms, and the storage shed in the rear had all appeared here intact.","Beyond the back door lay three acres of farmland. The soil was fertile and gave off the fresh fragrance of earth.","Beside it was a fishpond, its surface shimmering in the light and its water so clear that the bottom could be seen. Behind the pond stood a small mountain covered in lush greenery, its rolling slopes stretching into the distance.","The only difference was that a small spirit spring had appeared in one corner of the courtyard. Its water was crystal clear, with a faint white mist rising from it and a refreshing fragrance filling the air.","A pile of jade lay at the bottom of the spring. Among it were the jade bangle and jade pendants she recognized, along with many pieces of naturally formed jade in warm, lustrous colors. At a glance, they were clearly worth a fortune.","At the edge of the space, a thick layer of white mist shrouded everything. It seemed to stretch endlessly; she couldn’t reach its boundaries, nor could she enter it. The system explained that this was an area that had yet to be unlocked and that enough jade energy was required to open it.","Standing inside her own home, Jiang Yanyan felt instantly at ease.","No matter where she was, as long as she had the Yunhua Space, she had confidence and something to rely on.","She walked over to the spiritual spring, bent down, and scooped up a handful of spring water. It tasted sweet as it entered her mouth, and as it slid down her throat, a warm current instantly spread throughout her body. The slight pressure in her head caused by receiving the original host’s memories vanished in an instant, leaving her refreshed. Her body also felt incredibly light and comfortable.","As expected of spiritual spring water—the effects really were immediate.","Jiang Yanyan took another look around the supermarket, then inspected the fields and fish pond before finally feeling satisfied.","It was the middle of the night. The original host’s parents were away on a business trip overseas, and only she, the butler Uncle Chen, the housekeeper Auntie Chen, the driver, and a few others were in the villa. No one would disturb her.","She left the space and returned to the large bed in her bedroom. Although she wasn’t sleepy at all, she closed her eyes to rest and began organizing her plans for the days ahead.","There was still a week before school started. She intended to use these few days to get the Yunhua Space in order: buy enough seeds, farming tools, young livestock and poultry, and fish fry; fill the three acres of farmland with crops; stock the fish pond; and make full use of the back mountain. She would completely embark on her farming-and-hoarding lifestyle.","As for giving a speech as the student representative at the freshmen welcome ceremony after school began, that was nothing important. She wouldn’t take it to heart, much less give Song Ze any chance to approach her.","She spent the entire night awake. Just as dawn began to break, Jiang Yanyan woke up.","The moment she opened her eyes, the voice of System 0018 rang out in her mind:","[Ding—the host’s first sign-in is now available! Would you like to sign in?]","[Yes/No]","“Sign in.”","[The first sign-in bonus has been doubled. Rewards are being drawn...]","[Congratulations, Host! You have obtained an orange-tier reward: Stasis Space!]","[Congratulations, Host! You have obtained an orange-tier reward: the soul cultivation technique, Refining the Spirit!]","Two consecutive notification sounds instantly jolted Jiang Yanyan awake."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Spatial Fusion","paragraphs":["Two Orange Rewards? Or Two of Them?","[Stasis Space: Can be merged with the Yunhua Space to form an independent stasis zone. It can store any supplies, keeping them permanently fresh and at the proper temperature. Time is frozen within it, and nothing will ever spoil!]","[Soul Refining Art: A top-tier technique for cultivating the divine soul. It can temper the soul, strengthen the spirit, and protect against the risk of the soul being torn apart when traveling through space. With long-term cultivation, the strength of the divine soul can be increased!]","There was a rare trace of shock and envy in System 0018’s voice.","[Wow! Host, you’re incredibly lucky! You got two Orange rewards on your very first check-in. The odds of that are even lower than winning a hundred-million-yuan lottery jackpot!]","[The reward levels, from lowest to highest, are White, Green, Blue, Purple, Orange, Red, and Multicolored. Orange rewards are already considered rare.","Very few people draw Orange or Red rewards, and no one has ever drawn a Multicolored reward. You got two Orange rewards at once—you’re practically blessed by the god of luck!]","The corners of Zhang Yanyan’s lips lifted, and her mood brightened considerably.","The Stasis Space was perfect for stockpiling supplies. Her supermarket restocked automatically to begin with, and with the Stasis Space’s ability to keep everything permanently fresh, she would never have to worry about anything spoiling, no matter how much she stored.","The Soul Refining Art was even more essential. She would be traveling through countless minor worlds in the future, and as long as her soul was strong enough, she wouldn’t have to worry about being torn apart by space. Her safety would be guaranteed.","This first check-in had been an absolute windfall!","“Not bad. I’m very satisfied.” Zhang Yanyan barely managed to suppress her excitement, her mood thoroughly delighted.","Just then, someone gently knocked on the bedroom door. A warm voice came from outside.","“Miss, are you awake? Breakfast is ready. Come downstairs and eat.”","It was Auntie Chen, who had worked for the Zhang family for more than a decade. She had watched the original host grow up and was honest and dependable, treating the original host extremely well.","Zhang Yanyan immediately answered, “I’m awake, Auntie Chen. I’ll be down in a moment.”","She got out of bed and walked into the dressing room. When she opened the wardrobe, she found it filled with all kinds of designer clothes, handbags, and shoes. The dazzling array nearly made her eyes blur.","The original host had good taste. Her clothes were all simple and elegant. Zhang Yanyan chose a white cotton T-shirt and paired it with a pair of light-blue jeans—simple, comfortable, and practical.","After changing, she took another look at the jewelry box in the dressing room inside the space.","Only gold and silver jewelry remained inside: gold necklaces, gold bracelets, and gold rings, all arranged neatly and filling the box. Every piece of jade jewelry—the jade bangles, jade pendants, and jade drop ornaments—had vanished, leaving behind nothing but empty holders.","Zhang Yanyan understood immediately.","The jade had all been transferred by the system to the area beside the spirit spring in the Yunhua Space, where it had been used as the space’s initial source of energy.","From now on, she would keep the jewelry she retained in the dressing room. Whenever she wanted to charge the space, she could simply toss the jade into the spirit spring. The spring would automatically dissolve it and convert it into energy.","The Zhang family had more than enough money. She would have plenty of opportunities to buy more jade in the future and fill the Yunhua Space with energy, unlocking more of its functions.","Once she had finished getting ready, Zhang Yanyan opened the bedroom door and went downstairs.","The living room on the first floor was spacious and bright. In the dining room stood an exquisite solid-wood table, and Auntie Chen had already brought breakfast over: millet porridge, boiled eggs, steamed soup dumplings, and stir-fried vegetables. They were all dishes the original host loved—and exactly the kind of home cooking Zhang Yanyan enjoyed as well.","“Miss, it looks like you slept well last night. You seem to be in a good mood today.” Auntie Chen greeted her with a smile and took the coat Zhang Yanyan had casually draped over her arm. “You went to bed so late yesterday that I thought you’d sleep in today.”","“I couldn’t sleep, so I woke up early. I’m used to it.” Zhang Yanyan smiled and walked over to the table. Picking up her chopsticks, she said, “Auntie Chen’s cooking still smells as good as ever. I’m starving.”","The compliment made Auntie Chen beam.","“If you’re hungry, eat more. I simmered the millet porridge for over an hour, so it’s wonderfully soft and creamy. You’re about to start college, and you’re at the age when you’re still growing. You mustn’t go hungry.”","“Mm, I know.” Zhang Yanyan nodded and took small sips of the millet porridge. The warm porridge slid into her stomach, making her feel wonderfully comfortable.","“Your husband and wife are still abroad on a business trip,” Auntie Chen said as she placed a steamed soup dumpling in Zhang Yanyan’s bowl. “They said they won’t be able to come back until after school starts, when they have some free time. They specifically told me to take good care of you. If you’re lacking anything or need something, just let me know.”","“I know, Auntie Chen. I’m not lacking anything.” Zhang Yanyan paused, then added, “By the way, Auntie Chen, I’m going out today. I’ll drive myself, so there’s no need to send the chauffeur with me.”","She needed to buy seeds, farming tools, livestock and poultry, and fish fry so she could make full use of the three mu of farmland, the fishpond, and the back mountain in the Yunhua Space and begin her farming life. She didn’t want outsiders to know about these things, so driving herself was the safest option.","“All right. Be careful on the road, Miss.” Auntie Chen didn’t ask any questions and simply reminded her attentively, “Come back early. I’ll make your favorite braised fish for dinner.”","“Okay. Thank you, Auntie Chen.”","Zhang Yanyan quickly finished breakfast, said goodbye to Auntie Chen, picked up the car keys, and walked out of the villa.","The Zhang family’s home was a standalone estate. Several cars were parked in the garage, but Zhang Yanyan chose an unassuming white Audi Q5. It was easy to drive without being too flashy, making it suitable for running errands.","Once inside, she opened the navigation system and searched for Rong City’s largest suburban comprehensive agricultural market. After confirming the location of the market’s storage and logistics area, she stepped on the accelerator and drove there first.","The things she wanted to buy were varied and numerous. Her own car couldn’t possibly hold them all. More importantly, she couldn’t expose the existence of the Yunhua Space. Renting a temporary warehouse for transferring the goods was the safest option. That way, everything could be delivered to one place, and she could avoid prying eyes while quietly moving the supplies into the space.","When she arrived at the storage area, Zhang Yanyan went straight to the management office and stated her requirements clearly.","“I’d like to rent a temporary warehouse with a loading and unloading area for just one day. It needs to be large enough, have comprehensive security around the premises, and there must be no surveillance cameras inside.”","The staff quickly completed the arrangements for her. She chose an independent transfer warehouse located toward the inner part of the industrial park. It had security patrols around the clock and no cameras inside. After paying the rent and receiving the key, Zhang Yanyan drove to the agricultural market.","The agricultural supply market carried every kind of crop seed imaginable. Vegetables, grains, fruits, and miscellaneous cereals were all available in a dazzling variety.","Zhang Yanyan walked up to the largest and most reputable seed shop. The owner immediately greeted her enthusiastically.","“Miss, here to buy seeds? What kind are you looking for? We have everything. I guarantee a high germination rate and excellent yields!”","“I want all kinds of vegetable seeds—greens, cabbage, radishes, cucumbers, tomatoes, eggplants, chili peppers, and green beans. Two boxes of each.","“For fruit seeds, I want watermelons, melons, strawberries, and grapes—three boxes of each.","“And grain seeds: rice, wheat, corn...”","After listing everything in one breath, Zhang Yanyan added, “Also get me a complete set of farming tools—hoes, sickles, shovels, buckets, sprayers, all the best quality.","“And various types of agricultural machinery: tillers, seeders, harvesters, pesticide sprayers, threshers, and so on. Get the best models available for all of them.”","She would definitely need them in the future, so she might as well stock up now.","The shop owner’s eyes went wide. The young woman looked so delicate and refined—she hardly seemed like someone who worked the land. Who would have thought she would buy so many seeds and farming tools?","But the customer was always right, and the owner didn’t dare ask too many questions. He immediately nodded and bowed with a smile. “Of course, miss! I’ll pack everything up right away! I’ll make sure you get the best goods, and I’ll prepare a complete set of farming tools for you. The quality is absolutely guaranteed!”","Zhang Yanyan waited until the owner had checked and packed all the items, then paid the full amount. She left the address of the warehouse she had just rented, along with her phone number.","“Please deliver everything to this address before noon today. Someone will be there to receive the shipment.”","“No problem, no problem! I guarantee it’ll arrive on time!” the owner promised readily.","After leaving the seed shop, Zhang Yanyan went to the nearby nursery. She selected saplings of apples, pears, peaches, apricots, tangerines, oranges, cherries, blueberries, and various other fruit trees, buying dozens of each kind. She left the warehouse address as well and instructed the owner to deliver them together with the seeds before turning around and driving to the livestock and poultry market next door.","The market had every kind of young livestock imaginable—chickens, ducks, geese, cattle, sheep, and pigs. Their cries rose and fell one after another, making the place lively and noisy. The air carried a faint smell of livestock and feed.","Zhang Yanyan walked into the largest livestock breeding shop in the market, one with all the proper certifications and the best reputation.","“Boss, I’d like five pairs each of chickens, ducks, and geese, with one male and one female in every pair.","“Five pairs each of goats, sheep, beef cattle, and dairy cows as well. Ten piglets and ten calves, too. They all need to be healthy and disease-free.","“Also, prepare the appropriate amount of specialized feed for them, along with a complete set of vaccines and commonly used medicines for livestock and poultry.”","The owner was just as surprised, but he didn’t dare show the slightest bit of negligence. He hurriedly replied with a smile, “Don’t worry, miss! All my young animals are just over a month old and perfectly healthy. They’ve already received their basic vaccinations. I’ll prepare the most nutritious starter feed for them, and I’ll make sure you have a full range of medicines. I guarantee they’ll grow strong and sturdy!”","After Zhang Yanyan checked the types and quantities, she paid a deposit, left the warehouse address, and arranged for delivery before two in the afternoon. She specifically instructed the owner to arrange a temperature-controlled, well-ventilated vehicle so the young animals wouldn’t run into any problems on the way. The owner agreed repeatedly.","Her final stop was the aquatic products market. Zhang Yanyan found the largest wholesale seafood shop there and bought carp, grass carp, crucian carp, silver carp, perch, and various other fish fry, as well as hundreds of freshwater shrimp and crab seedlings. She required the owner to pack everything with continuous oxygenation and left the warehouse address once again, arranging delivery at roughly the same time as the livestock and poultry.","Once all her purchases had been finalized, Zhang Yanyan found a nearby café and sat down to wait for updates from the merchants. From time to time, she received delivery confirmations from the shop owners. Only after every merchant notified her that the goods had been delivered and signed for that afternoon did she get up and drive to the warehouse district.","When she arrived at the warehouse, she first walked around it to inspect the surroundings. After confirming that no one was nearby, she opened the warehouse door and went inside, locking it behind her.","The enormous warehouse was packed to the brim. Seeds, farming tools, fruit tree saplings, young livestock and poultry, fish fry, feed, and medicines were all stacked neatly, with even the unloading area filled to capacity.","Zhang Yanyan checked once more to make sure there were no surveillance cameras inside the warehouse and no outsiders present. Then, with a slight movement of her mind, every item in the warehouse vanished without a trace, all of it taken into her Yunhua Space.","After collecting everything, she locked the warehouse door, returned the key to the warehouse management office, and drove back to the Zhang family villa.","When ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍she entered the villa, Auntie Chen was cleaning the living room. Seeing her return, she greeted her with a smile.","“Miss, you’re back! Would you like some water and a little rest first? I can prepare dinner ahead of time.”","“No need, Auntie Chen. I’ll go back to my room and rest for a while. There’s no hurry about dinner.” Zhang Yanyan smiled and answered before quickly heading upstairs.","After locking her bedroom door, she activated her mind and entered the Yunhua Space.","She first took out all the jade and gemstone jewelry from her dressing room that she didn’t like or didn’t plan to keep, and threw it into the Spirit Spring.","The moment the jade entered the Spirit Spring, faint green streams of light appeared and slowly melted into the water. The energy within the space became a little stronger once again.","As for the jade jewelry she liked, she placed it carefully in the dressing room on the second floor of the space.","After finishing that, Zhang Yanyan rolled up her sleeves and began tending to her Yunhua Space.","She planned to use half of the three mu of farmland for vegetables and the other half for grain. With all the necessary farming tools at hand, she turned the soil, sowed the seeds, and watered the fields in an orderly fashion.","In the open land behind the mountain, she planted the fruit tree saplings. She dug holes, planted the saplings, filled the holes with soil, and watered them. Before long, the trees stood in neat rows.","She released all the fish fry into the pond. Countless lively shadows immediately appeared in the clear water.","In a clearing among the woods behind the mountain, she fenced off an area and placed the young chickens, ducks, and geese inside. At the foot of the mountain, she enclosed an even larger area and herded the calves, lambs, goats, and piglets into it. After scattering feed for them, she watched the little creatures chirping and hopping about energetically, and her heart filled with a sense of accomplishment.","With time moving ten times faster, it wouldn’t take more than a few days for the seeds to sprout, the fruit trees to take root, the livestock and poultry to grow, and the fish pond to yield a bountiful harvest.","Standing on the ridge between the fields in the Yunhua Space and gazing at everything brimming with life before her, Zhang Yanyan curved her lips into a gentle smile.","So what if the system had bonded with the wrong person? So what if she had transmigrated into the role of a cannon-fodder supporting female character?","With the Yunhua Space, she wasn’t losing out anyway. If she could take advantage of the situation a little, then she would take advantage of it as much as she could."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Eighteen","paragraphs":["Zhang Yanyan sat in a wooden chair in the side room, rocking leisurely back and forth.","Mist from the spirit spring drifted over, carrying with it a fresh, soothing fragrance of grass and trees.","She raised a hand and tapped her temple before calling out to the system.","“How exactly am I supposed to cultivate that Soul Refining Art?”","“I’ve never even come into contact with a cultivation technique before. I don’t have the slightest idea where to begin.”","【The Soul Refining Art is an advanced technique for cultivating the divine soul. Its cultivation threshold is relatively high.】","【The difficulty of the technique depends on the practitioner’s divine-soul aptitude. Your basic aptitude is acceptable.】","Zhang Yanyan raised an eyebrow and sat up straighter.","“Where is the technique stored? I can’t cultivate it out of thin air, can I?”","“I haven’t even seen the incantation. Where am I supposed to start?”","【The technique is stored in the system space. The host only needs to silently think, “Extract the Soul Refining Art.”】","【Once you silently recite “Extract the Soul Refining Art,” the technique will transform into a stream of light and imprint itself onto your divine soul.】","【There is no need to memorize it by rote. It will directly merge with your consciousness.】","Hearing this, Zhang Yanyan obediently followed the instructions.","She squeezed her eyes shut and silently spoke the command in her mind.","“Extract the Soul Refining Art.”","The next moment, a gentle white stream of light suddenly exploded outward.","Fine as silken thread, it slipped through the space between her eyebrows and plunged straight into the depths of her divine soul.","Within her originally empty mind, an ancient cultivation manual radiating a soft glow unfurled in an instant.","The characters were written in archaic seal script, yet, strangely enough, she could understand every one of them.","Each character carried a warm, gentle power that slowly merged into her consciousness.","Zhang Yanyan drew a deep breath and followed the instructions of the technique, sitting cross-legged.","She chose a slab of bluestone beside the spirit spring. The ground was cool and clean.","The spirit spring’s vapor curled around her, perfectly suited to nourishing the divine soul and assisting her cultivation.","Honestly, this place had been chosen perfectly. It had everything going for it.","Following the guidance of the Soul Refining Art, she emptied her mind of all thoughts.","She cast aside distracting thoughts and concentrated her mind on the core of her divine soul between her brows.","Bit by bit, she guided the free divine-soul energy in the air into her body.","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍first, the process was extremely clumsy.","Her divine soul was like a rusted gear, sluggish and laborious to turn.","Sweat beaded on Zhang Yanyan’s forehead, but she gritted her teeth and refused to stop.","Fortunately, time moved ten times faster inside Yunhua Space.","Only half an hour passed in the outside world, while five hours had already gone by inside the space.","Again and again, she pondered the incantation. Again and again, she tried to circulate the technique.","From rough and halting movements, it gradually became smooth.","From being able to draw in only a thread of feeble energy, she progressed to circulating it through half a minor cycle.","The sluggishness within her divine soul slowly faded, replaced by a refreshing sense of fullness.","Several more hours passed. By then, an entire day had gone by inside the space.","Zhang Yanyan slowly opened her eyes, a faint golden glimmer flashing through them.","She had finally managed to grasp the Soul Refining Art.","The cultivation route now circulated steadily within her divine soul.","Thread after thread of divine-soul energy flowed in an endless cycle, nourishing her entire soul.","The slight weariness brought on by her transmigration had vanished completely.","She stretched, and the joints in her bones gave off a series of soft clicks.","Her whole body felt light and relaxed, and even her thoughts had become noticeably sharper.","Now that she thought about it, all her earlier worries about being unable to learn the technique had been completely unnecessary.","With a thought, Zhang Yanyan directly left Yunhua Space.","Her luxurious bedroom came into view, sunlight pouring in through the bay window.","She glanced at the electronic clock beside the bed. It was only seven-thirty in the morning.","The moment she steadied herself, the system’s notification sounded.","【Host, today’s check-in is now available. Would you like to check in?】","Leaning against the headboard, Zhang Yanyan casually replied, “Check in.”","【Check-in successful. Today is an ordinary day, so ordinary daily rewards will be issued.】","【Green-tier reward obtained: Ten pounds of premium Wuchang rice.】","【Green-tier reward obtained: One package of naturally organic vegetables.】","【White-tier reward obtained: Five pure-cotton towels.】","【White-tier reward obtained: One package of disposable medical masks.】","【White-tier reward obtained: One household cleaning set.】","【Rewards have been automatically stored in the Stasis Space.】","Zhang Yanyan pursed her lips, though she wasn’t disappointed.","Yesterday had been her first check-in, and the doubled benefits had resulted in an orange-tier grand prize.","Getting two green-tier rewards from an ordinary daily check-in was already pretty good.","These daily supplies were better than nothing.","Time was frozen in the Stasis Space, so nothing would spoil no matter how long it was stored.","It was always useful to stockpile things. There was no reason not to take them.","As she leaned against the headboard and finally had a moment to relax, she suddenly remembered something.","“By the way, do you have a name?”","“How am I supposed to address you normally? I can’t keep calling you ‘System’ forever.”","【I am Check-In System 0018 under the Main System.】","【I have no personal name, only a work identification number.】","Zhang Yanyan mulled it over for a moment. The number was too awkward to say.","“0018 is too troublesome. I’ll call you Eighteen.”","“It’s easy to remember and rolls off the tongue. That’s what I’ll call you from now on.”","【Acceptable.】","Zhang Yanyan smiled and tossed out another question that had been bothering her.","“I’ve never really understood what happened with my transmigration.”","“You said earlier that there were no compulsory missions, so why did you bind yourself to me and make me transmigrate?”","【I am a laid-back Check-In System. My core responsibilities are to change the original host’s fate and provide daily check-in rewards.】","【The Main System oversees many different types of task systems, each with its own duties.】","【Villain Redemption System: Clear the villain’s name, reverse their fate, and rewrite their tragic ending.】","【Supporting-Female-Character Comeback System: Help cannon-fodder female characters slap the protagonists in the face and turn their lives around.】","【Apocalypse Survival System: Lead the host in developing wastelands after the apocalypse while upholding the bottom line of survival.】","【Palace and Household Struggle System: Assist the host in gaining a firm foothold in the imperial harem or a powerful household.】","【Entertainment Industry Comeback System: Turn the host into a top celebrity and sweep up the industry’s best resources.】","【Esports Ascension System: Help the host dominate the professional arena and win a global championship.】","【Ancient Imperial Examination System: Accompany the host from being a humble scholar all the way to becoming the top-ranked candidate and receiving a noble title.】","【Interstellar Development System: Travel to an interstellar planet, cultivate new territory, and build a home.】","【Adorable Pet Development System: Care for special pets and unlock their innate supernatural abilities.】","【Quick-Transmigration Revenge System: Help the original host take revenge and punish the scumbag men, vile women, and villains.】","【Mysticism Salvation System: Use feng shui and talismans to resolve crises and protect the people of an entire region.】","【Gourmet Business System: Open a restaurant and become a leading magnate in the industry.】","【Campus Domination System: Help the host rise from the bottom to become a top student and the center of attention at school.】","【Mecha Combat System: Pilot mechas across the stars and wage war on countless battlefields.】","【Antique Appraisal System: Identify ancient treasures and accumulate wealth and connections.】","Zhang Yanyan’s eyes widened as she listened, and she clicked her tongue in wonder.","“Good grief, there are so many systems. They really cover every possible niche.”","“So your Check-In System is basically the most useless one of the lot?”","【The Check-In System has no compulsory missions and no punishment mechanism. It is a leisure-oriented system.】","【The host only needs to protect the original host’s family and change their tragic fate.】","【The host can receive rewards through daily check-ins. Living a peaceful and stable life is the system’s core requirement.】","【Its drawback is that points are earned slowly, and the system takes a long time to level up.】","【Compared with comeback and revenge systems, it has fewer missions and poses no threat to the host’s life.】","【Its guiding principle is peace, stability, and a laid-back approach to survival.】","Zhang Yanyan nodded repeatedly, deeply agreeing.","“Exactly. Nothing is more important than staying safe.”","“I don’t want to fight and kill. Living a peaceful life is the best.”","“Your laid-back system was practically made for me.”","All she had ever wanted was to guard her space, grow crops, and stockpile supplies.","Stay away from the scumbag man and the shameless woman, protect the Zhangs' parents, and live a comfortable life.","As for whether she could level up through points, Zhang Yanyan simply didn’t care.","She and the Check-In System chatted for a while longer about other things.","Zhang Yanyan had figured out all the rules of the Check-In System.","She committed the reward tiers, uses for points, and conditions for unlocking the space to memory, one by one.","Just as they had nearly finished talking, a soft knock sounded at the door.","Auntie Chen’s kindly voice came from outside, gentle and warm.","“Miss, are you awake? Breakfast is ready. Come downstairs and eat.”","Zhang Yanyan immediately called back, threw off the covers, and got out of bed.","“I’m awake, Auntie Chen. I’ll be right down.”","She walked into the dressing room and casually picked out a pale pink dress.","The dress was made of pure cotton, loose and comfortable, with a simple design.","Paired with a pair of white canvas shoes, it gave her a fresh, girl-next-door look.","There was none of the spoiled arrogance one might expect from a wealthy heiress; it suited her personality perfectly.","She simply tied her hair into a low ponytail and went without makeup.","The original owner had been beautiful to begin with, with fair skin and delicate features.","She was already striking enough without makeup.","After opening the bedroom door, she made her way down the spiral staircase.","On the solid-wood table in the dining room on the first floor sat a steaming breakfast spread.","Millet and pumpkin porridge, steamed dumplings, boiled eggs, chilled cucumber salad, and small milk buns.","Everything was light, tasty, and home-style, with an enticing aroma wafting through the room."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: The Four Great Families","paragraphs":["Auntie Chen stood nearby, smiling as she watched her.","“Miss, you look lovely in that outfit today.”","“Thank you, Auntie Chen. You look well too. It seems you got a good night’s rest.”","Zhang Yanyan pulled out a chair and sat down, picking up her spoon to scoop up a mouthful of porridge.","The porridge was soft, fragrant, and sweet, with the pumpkin’s natural sweetness melting into the aroma of the rice.","“Auntie Chen’s cooking is always so delicious. I can never get enough.”","Pleased by the compliment, Auntie Chen’s eyes curved into a smile as she handed over a plate of steamed dumplings.","“If you like it, eat more. You’ll be starting university soon, so you need to keep yourself well nourished. Your husband and madam are busy overseas and specifically asked me to take good care of you.”","Zhang Yanyan bit into a steamed dumpling and nodded.","The wrapper was thin and the filling generous. The pork-and-cabbage filling was wonderfully fresh.","“I know. Auntie Chen is the best to me.”","As they were eating, footsteps sounded from the entryway.","Uncle Chen, the butler, walked in wearing a perfectly pressed black suit.","Uncle Chen had worked for the Zhang family for twenty years. He was utterly loyal and handled matters with great efficiency and care.","He walked over to the dining table and gave a slight bow.","“Good morning, Miss. I just finished a video call with your parents.”","Zhang Yanyan set down her spoon and looked up at him.","“How are my parents? Is the business negotiation going smoothly? When will they be coming home?”","[The overseas cooperation between your parents and their partners has reached a preliminary agreement.]","[The subsequent signing procedures are complicated, and they will be unable to return in the short term.]","[They originally planned to come back before the start of the semester to accompany you, but that plan can no longer be fulfilled.]","Uncle Chen spoke respectfully, relaying every detail truthfully.","“Your parents asked me to tell you that you mustn’t shortchange yourself. Your father has already spoken with the university, so you have nothing to worry about.”","Warmth spread through Zhang Yanyan’s heart. The original owner’s parents truly loved their daughter.","They were simply busy with their careers and had little time to accompany her.","But their love and affection for her had never been lacking.","“I understand, Uncle Chen. Tell them to focus on their business and not worry about me. I’m an adult now. I can take care of myself.”","Uncle Chen nodded before asking about her preparations for university.","“Miss, would you like us to arrange for someone to purchase your luggage and daily necessities? Do you need us to prepare bedding and other supplies for the dormitory at Tengyuan University?”","Zhang Yanyan shook her head. She had never intended to live in the dormitory.","There were too many people, too little privacy, and no freedom. It was far more comfortable to live on her own.","Besides, living near the characters involved in the plot would make it easy for them to pester her. It simply wasn’t worth the trouble.","“No need to prepare anything for the dormitory. I probably won’t be living on campus. Uncle Chen, do we have any properties near Tengyuan University? It doesn’t need to be too large. Somewhere quiet and private that’s convenient for everyday living would be perfect.”","At once, Uncle Chen understood. He immediately listed the options.","“Yes, Miss. The family purchased three properties nearby in advance, all reserved for you while you attend university. They’re ready for you to move in at any time.”","“The first is a small detached villa with two and a half floors, a garden, and a private garage. It occupies more than three hundred square meters, has European-style décor, and is only a ten-minute drive from Tengyuan University’s main entrance.”","“The second is a two-hundred-square-meter luxury apartment on a high floor. It has an expansive view, round-the-clock security, and is fully furnished and ready for immediate occupancy.”","“The third is a five-hundred-square-meter duplex apartment with two floors and ample space.”","All three properties had been prepared by the Zhang family long ago.","They had made sure to have alternatives in case the original owner found dormitory life uncomfortable.","Zhang Yanyan searched through the original owner’s memories and indeed found some vague recollection of them.","The original owner had never visited any of the properties, however, so she had no real idea what they were like.","After a moment’s thought, Zhang Yanyan chose the small villa.","The luxury apartment and duplex were both located in residential buildings, where there would be too many people and too much noise.","A detached villa, with its own private grounds, would be quiet and secluded.","Its layout also happened to resemble the building she had constructed in Yunhua Space, so she would be accustomed to living there.","“I’ll take the two-and-a-half-story villa. Uncle Chen, arrange for people to clean and furnish it as soon as possible. Once the semester begins, I’ll be living there permanently.”","Uncle Chen immediately agreed and took out the tablet he carried with him to make a note.","“Of course, Miss. I’ll arrange for the housekeepers to clean the property and handle the furnishings at once. Would you like it renovated, or should we keep the existing style?”","“No need for a complete renovation. That would take too long. Just furnish it simply in the same style as my current bedroom. You can make the arrangements for the bedding, furniture, and so on.”","She liked the décor in her current rooms and saw no need to go to the trouble of changing it.","Zhang Yanyan couldn’t be bothered with the hassle. Replicating the existing style would be the simplest option.","Besides, she didn’t have any particularly strong preferences when it came to interior design.","“Do you have anyone specific in mind for the furnishings and setup, Miss? Or should I select people directly from the manor’s household staff?” Uncle Chen asked.","Zhang Yanyan thought for a moment. There were many servants at the manor, but she was only familiar with most of them and wasn’t particularly close to any.","Auntie Chen was the only one who had cared for her for many years. She understood her habits, was attentive, and could be trusted.","“Have Auntie Chen go with me. She’s an excellent cook and knows my daily routine well. Having her there will save me a lot of trouble.”","Auntie Chen’s face lit up at once.","“Of course, Miss! I can pack up and leave whenever you like. I guarantee I’ll take excellent care of everything.”","Uncle Chen gave a slight nod and considered the size of the villa before saying, “The detached villa is moderately sized, so there won’t be too many daily chores. With Auntie Chen handling your meals and daily needs, one additional housekeeper to take care of cleaning and the household work will be enough.”","“As for security, we can assign two personal bodyguards to handle your day-to-day safety, along with one dedicated driver for your transportation. It will keep the staff lean without compromising your comfort. Does that arrangement sound suitable?”","Zhang Yanyan thought the arrangement was just right. It was neither extravagant nor lacking in comfort, so she nodded immediately.","“That works. Go ahead with that arrangement. You can choose the people yourself. As long as they’re efficient, discreet, steady, and don’t cause unnecessary trouble, that’s all that matters.”","Uncle Chen agreed at once. After thinking for a moment, he suggested someone.","“Aunt Wang from the manor would be the most suitable. She’s efficient and honest. She used to serve the old madam, follows the rules, and rarely speaks unnecessarily. She’s exceptionally reliable.”","Zhang Yanyan searched through the original owner’s memories. Aunt Wang was indeed an honest woman who was quiet, hardworking, and capable of keeping the household in perfect order.","“All right. It’ll be just Auntie Chen and Aunt Wang. Please finalize the bodyguards and driver as well, and have everyone head to the villa and settle in as soon as possible. Everything must be ready within two days. Once the semester starts, I’ll move in directly.”","“Yes, Miss. I’ll make the arrangements immediately.”","Uncle Chen bowed and turned to handle the matter.","His footsteps were light and measured. Uncle Chen had always been highly efficient, and Zhang Yanyan trusted him completely.","She continued eating breakfast, feeling considerably more at ease.","With a private villa of her own, she would be able to avoid a great deal of unnecessary trouble.","After finishing breakfast, she said goodbye to Auntie Chen.","Then she returned to her bedroom on the second floor and locked the door behind her.","She intended to first look into the basic situation here and the power structure of Rongcheng, matching each family’s name with the faces of its members. That way, she wouldn’t embarrass herself later.","After all, she was the daughter of one of Rongcheng’s top wealthy families.","It would be awkward if she went out and, despite being a local, knew nothing about the influential families in her own city.","What if she ran into someone from another prominent household and failed to recognize them?","She walked over to the desk and opened the original owner’s laptop.","It was the latest top-of-the-line model and booted up almost instantly.","She clicked through the files and began looking into the distribution of power among Rongcheng’s major families.","Detailed information soon appeared on the screen.","As ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍one of the country’s first-tier cities, Rongcheng had a highly developed economy and was home to countless wealthy families.","At the very top were the four families universally recognized as Rongcheng’s most powerful.","At the top of the list was the Chen family, whose core businesses were finance and aviation.","With assets worth trillions, they had the deepest roots and the broadest reach.","The family was headed by Chen Jingshan, a ruthless man whose influence in the business world was second to none.","In second place was the Lin family, whose main industries were new energy and pharmaceuticals.","Their research and development capabilities were among the best, making them the leading force in emerging industries.","The family was headed by Lin Zhenghong, a rising star with a razor-sharp eye for opportunity.","Third was the Zhang family—the family Zhang Yanyan belonged to.","The Zhang Group’s core businesses included real estate, technology, and chain retail.","With assets worth hundreds of billions, they controlled nearly half of Rongcheng’s real estate market.","Fourth was the Gu family, whose businesses spanned luxury goods, hotels, and entertainment.","They controlled Rongcheng’s high-end consumer market and had an extraordinarily wide network of connections.","The family was headed by Gu Yanzhi, a young man who nonetheless wielded an iron fist."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Divine Refinement Art","paragraphs":["Zhang Yanyan went through the materials one by one, committing every detail to memory.","She opened the photographs and profiles of the heads of each family, matching every face to its name so that she would not be discourteous if they crossed paths in the future.","As the Zhang heiress, learning about the connections and power structures within wealthy circles had been part of her education since childhood. The original host was merely young, with most of her attention focused on her financial management studies in preparation for taking over the family group in the future. She was by no means an ignorant young heiress who knew nothing of the world.","Her parents currently handled the family business in its entirety. Although she had not yet become directly involved, she was far from completely uninformed.","Now that she had taken the original host’s place, she had to gain a thorough understanding of Rong City’s power structure. As a member of one of the city’s most elite families, she did not need to know every detail, but she had to be aware of the important players.","To put it bluntly, with Zhang Yanyan’s current status, she was the one others needed to treat with caution and consideration. The only people who could make Zhao Yanyan exercise caution were a very small number indeed.","She spent the entire morning sorting through the connections and influence networks of everyone from the branches of third-rate families to the core members of the Four Great Families of Rong City. Every person she might come into contact with was matched with the corresponding memories in her mind.","By the time she finished going through all the information, it was nearly noon.","Her stomach began to rumble faintly. She had just risen to go downstairs when someone gently knocked on the bedroom door. Auntie Chen’s warm voice came from outside.","“Miss, it’s lunchtime. What would you like to eat? I’ll make it for you in the kitchen.”","“We have fresh ribs, fish, and vegetables. I can make any of them.”","Leaning back in her chair, Zhang Yanyan casually named a few dishes.","“Braised ribs, stir-fried lettuce, and tomato-and-egg-drop soup. Rice for the main dish. Keep it simple.”","“All right, Miss. I’ll get started right away.”","Auntie Chen readily agreed and hurried off toward the kitchen. Zhang Yanyan gazed at the closed door and quietly breathed a sigh of relief.","With her parents away, meals were actually more relaxing. She did not have to worry about putting on an act or accidentally revealing that something was wrong. She could simply eat whatever she wanted.","She rose and walked to the window, looking out over the enormous estate.","The Zhang family’s ancestral residence occupied several hundred acres. As one of Rong City’s top families, the estate was grand beyond measure, with gardens, lawns, swimming pools, pavilions, and viewing platforms arranged throughout the grounds.","There were dozens of people assigned specifically to her side of the household, including nannies, personal bodyguards, servants, a butler, a private gardener, and a family doctor. Each had their own duties, and everything was handled quietly and flawlessly.","Her parents had their own assistants, bodyguards, and support staff as well, ensuring that every aspect of the family’s internal and external affairs was managed without the slightest negligence.","Such a life in an elite family looked glamorous on the surface, but in reality, it came with complicated rules and an enormous amount to learn.","Zhang Yanyan let out a soft sigh before turning and entering the Cloudlight Dimension. With time moving ten times faster inside, it was the perfect place to cultivate. The Soul Refining Art had only just reached the entry level, and she needed to focus and hone it properly.","Within the dimension, mist drifted above the spirit spring. The jade stone beside it slowly released a gentle, soothing energy, while the seeds planted in the furrows had already sprouted tender green shoots.","The tenfold growth rate was truly no exaggeration. In barely a day, the seeds had broken through the soil. In a few more days, she would be able to eat fresh vegetables.","She sat cross-legged beside the spirit spring and closed her eyes, circulating the Soul Refining Art. The power of her soul gradually grew stronger, and her five senses became increasingly sharp. She could clearly perceive even the slightest movement within the dimension.","The feeling of having complete control over herself brought her immense peace of mind.","Time quietly passed in the outside world. After Auntie Chen finished preparing lunch, she waited downstairs for a long while, never daring to go up and disturb her.","It was not until after one in the afternoon that Zhang Yanyan finally emerged from her cultivation. Glancing at the time, she realized with surprise that she had long since missed lunch. She hurriedly got up and went downstairs.","“Auntie Chen, I got so caught up in what I was doing that I lost track of time. I’m sorry to have kept you waiting.”","Auntie Chen did not mind in the slightest. Smiling, she took the dishes from the insulated food container and placed them on the table. They were still steaming hot.","“It’s nothing, Miss. It’s good for young people to stay busy. The food’s been kept warm. Go ahead and eat.”","The braised ribs glistened with a rich red sheen and gave off an enticing aroma. The stir-fried lettuce was crisp and green, while the tomato-and-egg-drop soup was tangy, sweet, and appetizing.","They were all simple, home-style dishes, yet they filled her with a warm sense of comfort.","Zhang Yanyan picked up her chopsticks and ate in large mouthfuls. Having been hungry for half the day, she found everything especially delicious.","Auntie Chen sat beside her and watched with an affectionate smile, repeatedly reminding her to slow down and offering to serve her more if she was still hungry.","“There’s no need to trouble yourself, Auntie Chen. I can come downstairs on my own.” Zhang Yanyan answered around a mouthful of food. “I’ll be more careful next time and won’t miss mealtime again.”","She finished the lunch feeling thoroughly satisfied. Afterward, she returned to her bedroom and began planning her next steps.","Although the jade energy in the dimension was abundant, she could not simply deplete it without replenishing the supply. The spirit spring required a constant source of energy to keep operating, so she had to stockpile a large amount in advance.","For the next two days, she planned to focus on purchasing jade. The finest pieces would be kept for wearing and nurturing, while ordinary-quality jade would be fed directly into the spirit spring to replenish its energy.","The Zhang family was wealthy enough that this expense amounted to little more than a drop in the bucket.","Rong City was filled with jade wholesalers, high-end jewelry stores, and private jade galleries. By purchasing a large supply, she could ensure that the dimension continued to operate steadily while also accumulating enough energy to unlock the undeveloped regions.","At the thought, Zhang Yanyan’s eyes lit up. Stockpiling supplies, cultivating, and quietly guarding her family business—that was the kind of comfortable life she wanted.","Leaning against the headboard, she took out her phone and searched for Rong City’s jade markets. She marked the locations of the largest wholesale market, the high-end flagship stores, and the private jade galleries one by one, planning to set out first thing the next morning.","System ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍Eighteen remained quietly in her consciousness and never took the initiative to disturb her. It only spoke up when it was time to check in. Such a laid-back system was practically the ideal partner.","Looking at the store information on her phone, Zhang Yanyan’s lips curved into a faint smile.","Staying away from troublesome people, protecting her dimension and her family—this life was a hundred times more comfortable than her old one.","She did not enter the dimension again. Instead, she flipped through the original host’s high school photo album. The girl in the photographs was youthful and shy, with pure, innocent eyes, yet she had been swept up in the plot and ultimately met a miserable end.","Sunlight streamed through the window and fell across her body, warm and gentle. With the years peaceful and serene, Zhang Yanyan closed her eyes for a brief rest. The plans in her heart had already become perfectly clear.","First thing tomorrow morning, she would go to Rong City’s largest jade wholesale market and purchase ordinary jade in bulk to fill the dimension’s energy reserves.","In the afternoon, she would visit high-end jewelry stores and select several fine jade pieces for her own use and as a backup.","The day after that, she would go to private jade galleries to search for some less common rough stones or antique jade, ensuring that her jade reserves were more than sufficient.","Once she had accumulated enough jade, she would move into the small villa near Tengyuan and quietly wait for the start of the school term, completely breaking free from the original host’s tragic path.","As for giving the speech as the freshman representative, it would merely be a formality. She could handle it with ease.","If Song Ze came up to her again, she would simply reject him. Did she have to accept every person who confessed their feelings to her?","And if, after being rejected, he still refused to take the hint and harassed her persistently, that would be easy enough to deal with.","She let out a soft laugh and lightly tapped her fingers against the headboard.","She was the Zhang heiress, with bodyguards accompanying her wherever she went. If he truly angered her, she could simply call in reinforcements.","If he really continued pestering her without end, giving him a few beatings to vent her frustration would not be a problem. She would let him properly experience the confidence that came with being an heiress of a wealthy family.","She lightly touched the center of her brow. The Soul Refining Art continued to circulate slowly within her soul, sending a faint warmth throughout her body. Then she called out to her system.","“Eighteen, will I still be controlled by the original plot in the future? Will fate continue to follow the same script?”","【Host, rest assured. You are an outsider’s soul, and you came here precisely to rewrite the original host’s fate. The shackles of the plot have already lost their effect. You will absolutely never be controlled by it again. Otherwise, it would go against the very purpose of your transmigration and rebirth.】","With that definite answer, Zhang Yanyan was finally at ease.","So what if she had transmigrated into the role of a cannon-fodder female supporting character? With the Yunhua Space, a check-in system, the Cultivation Formula of Soul Refinement, and the backing of the powerful Zhang family, she alone would decide the path ahead.","Before bed, she made a point of reminding Eighteen, “Remember to wake me tomorrow morning so I can go buy some jade. Don’t let me oversleep and delay anything important.”","【Morning wake-up reminder set. Host will be awakened on time.】","Reassured, Zhang Yanyan closed her eyes and soon drifted into a deep sleep. In her dreams, there was only the peaceful, ordinary life she had always longed for.","This was the life she wanted.","With trump cards in hand, she could deal with whatever came her way. She didn’t need to hide or run away—she could still live the life of a winner.","When she woke, the sun outside was already sinking toward the horizon. The evening breeze drifted in through the gauze window, carrying a faint floral fragrance. Zhang Yanyan stretched, feeling every muscle and joint in her body loosen and relax.","Auntie Chen’s gentle voice floated up from downstairs, calling her to dinner.","“Miss, come down and eat! I made your favorite braised fish tonight, along with some mushroom soup. It’s wonderfully fresh—come down and have a taste.”","Zhang Yanyan answered with a smile and turned to head downstairs.","Her steps were light, and her spirits were bright."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Jade","paragraphs":["Just as dawn began to break, the familiar mechanical voice exploded in her consciousness right on schedule.","【Host, the morning reminder has been triggered. Today’s check-in is officially open!】","Zhang Yanyan rubbed her messy hair and sat up in bed.","She had stayed up until late the previous night cultivating the Soul Refining Art, yet her mind felt not the slightest bit groggy. On the contrary, it was exceptionally clear.","“Check in, check in. Hurry up and give me my rewards. Stop dawdling.”","She leaned against the headboard and let out a small yawn, her tone lazy and languid.","【Check-in successful! Today’s rewards are being randomly drawn...】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a blue-tier reward: Supreme Financial Trading Skills!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a green-tier reward: Premium Organic Food Gift Pack ×1!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a green-tier reward: Complete Set of Intelligent Fully Automated Agricultural Machinery ×1!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a white-tier reward: Custom Luxury Skincare Set ×1!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a white-tier reward: High-End Office Stationery Gift Box ×1!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a white-tier reward: Portable Outdoor Water Purification Equipment ×3!】","【Congratulations, Host! You have received a white-tier reward: Complete Luxury Camping Set ×1!】","Zhang Yanyan’s eyes lit up in an instant.","The blue-tier reward was actually supreme financial trading skills?","It was practically tailored to her heart’s desires!","The original owner had already planned to major in financial management at university and take over the Zhang family’s business in the future. This was precisely the ability she had been lacking.","With a slight movement of her thoughts, all the rewards were instantly put away.","Every last one was stored in the time-frozen section of the Yunhua Space.","Time was completely still there. Even if something was left inside for a hundred years, it would remain as fresh and new as the day it entered.","There was nowhere more suitable for stockpiling supplies and storing treasures.","The next second, an enormous amount of financial knowledge surged into her mind.","From short-term stock trading to long-term capital planning, from corporate risk management to cross-industry venture investment decisions, dense streams of information poured in. Yet none of it felt obscure or difficult to understand.","It was as if these skills had been carved into her bones from birth. She understood everything at a glance.","Zhang Yanyan smacked her lips, unable to stop herself from secretly rejoicing.","With this skill, managing the Zhang family’s businesses in the future would be as easy as adding wings to a tiger.","The green-tier rewards were even more perfectly suited to her farming ambitions.","The premium organic food gift pack contained all kinds of rare fruits, vegetables, grains, and beans.","The complete set of intelligent agricultural machinery could plow fields, sow seeds, and water crops with the push of a button.","She had only just finished tidying up the farmland in her space yesterday, and today the system had delivered an entire set of machines. This system understood her far too well.","Once she had the seeds ready, she could practically leave everything to the machines.","The white-tier rewards looked ordinary... and, well, they really were fairly ordinary.","The custom skincare set was just right for the original owner’s delicate skin.","The high-end stationery gift box would come in handy for taking notes in university.","As for the portable water purifiers and camping equipment, she would no longer have to worry about them when she went out traveling in the future.","Zhang Yanyan happily went through all the rewards one by one.","To think that a routine daily check-in could produce a blue-tier grand prize. Her luck was simply unbeatable.","She stretched luxuriously, and a series of soft cracks sounded from her joints.","Today, she had only one main objective—","Buy up as much jade as possible, fill the Yunhua Space’s energy reserves to the brim, and see what the space would look like after upgrading.","The spiritual spring’s operation and the expansion of the space all relied on jade. She absolutely could not allow the supply to run out.","She threw back the covers, got out of bed, and walked into the bathroom in her slippers.","The original owner’s bedroom came with its own private bathroom, decorated with exquisite and comfortable furnishings.","She washed her face with warm water, instantly dispelling the last trace of drowsiness.","When changing clothes, she did not choose any of the flashy designer dresses.","Instead, she picked out a loose, neat, light-apricot cotton casual outfit.","She paired it with a pair of white sneakers—convenient for making a quick getaway and not at all eye-catching.","She casually tied her hair into a low ponytail and went downstairs bare-faced.","The original owner had already been naturally pretty, with delicate, pleasing features and skin so fair it seemed to glow.","Without makeup, she looked even cleaner and more comfortable than she would have in heavy cosmetics.","When Zhang Yanyan reached the first floor, Uncle Chen was already waiting in the living room.","He wore a crisp black suit and stood perfectly straight, his manner respectful.","Zhang Yanyan went straight to the point without any unnecessary small talk.","“Uncle Chen, I’m going to purchase a batch of rough jadeite today. Arrange two capable bodyguards for me, and have two heavy-duty cargo trucks prepared.”","Her tone was casual, as if she were simply asking to buy a few pounds of vegetables.","Uncle Chen did not ask a single question. He immediately bowed slightly and replied, “Of course, Miss.”","A wealthy family’s butler understood the rules better than anyone. If something was not his place to ask about, he would never say a word.","In less than three minutes, two tall, well-built bodyguards were standing by the entrance.","The one on the left was called A-Li. He had a sturdy build and a sharp gaze.","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍one on the right was called A-Hu. He was calm and reserved, with quick, capable movements.","Both men were veteran bodyguards who had served the Zhang family for many years. They were loyal and dependable.","Uncle Li had also prepared the vehicles well in advance, parking them outside the estate.","The main car was an understated black Bentley, both comfortable and secure.","Two heavy-duty cargo trucks followed behind it. Their spacious cargo compartments could handle a huge load with ease.","Zhang Yanyan nodded in satisfaction. Having more people around really did make things more convenient.","It saved her from running back and forth herself and wearing herself out moving things.","Just as she was about to leave, Auntie Chen came hurrying after her with an insulated food bag.","“Miss, eat something if you get hungry on the road. Don’t let yourself go without food. There are steamed dumplings and warm milk inside, both of them your favorites.”","Auntie Chen’s face was full of affection, and her voice was soft and gentle.","Zhang Yanyan accepted the bag, her heart warming.","She smiled and replied, “I know, Auntie Chen. I’ll be back early.”","She turned around and took her seat in the back of the Bentley. A-Li and A-Hu each got behind the wheel of one of the cargo trucks and followed behind.","The three vehicles left the Zhang family estate smoothly and headed toward Rong City’s Jewelry Plaza.","Zhang Yanyan leaned back against the soft seat and closed her eyes to rest.","At the same time, she reviewed the financial trading knowledge she had just acquired.","The complicated logic behind capital operations and corporate management was now crystal clear in her mind, as though she had studied it for more than a decade.","She could not help sighing inwardly. This blue-tier reward was truly worth it.","More than half an hour later, the vehicles stopped in front of the most prestigious jewelry store in Rong City.","The store belonged to a high-end brand under the Gu Group and specialized in top-grade jade jewelry. Ordinary people could not even get through its doors.","The moment the car came to a stop, Manager Wang led a group of employees out to greet them.","He recognized the Zhang family’s car and knew the identity of the Zhang heiress even better.","He bent at the waist in a bow so deep it was nearly ninety degrees, his attitude respectful to the extreme.","“Miss Zhang, what an honor to have you visit us! We apologize for failing to welcome you sooner. Please, come right in!”","Manager Wang personally led the way, not daring to show the slightest hint of negligence.","He escorted Zhang Yanyan all the way to the private VIP room on the top floor.","The VIP room was both luxurious and elegant, furnished with European-style carved sofas.","Fresh imported fruit and delicate pastries had been arranged on the crystal coffee table.","An employee served freshly brewed Dragon Well tea, its fragrance curling gently through the air. The service was impeccable.","Zhang Yanyan sank into the sofa and shifted comfortably in her seat.","Getting straight to the point, she told Manager Wang what she wanted.","“Bring out all the top-grade jade jewelry and ornaments in your store. Also prepare a large quantity of ordinary-quality jade roughs and cutoffs. I have an important use for them. I’ll take as much as you have—everything.”","Her tone was mild, yet it carried the unmistakable confidence unique to a wealthy heiress.","Manager Wang’s eyes lit up instantly. He knew a massive sale had just landed in his lap.","He hurriedly waved for the employees to retrieve the goods from the back, not daring to delay for even a moment.","Before long, trays covered in dazzling jade jewelry were brought out one after another.","There was a mutton-fat white jade bangle, warm and smooth to the touch, with such abundant luster that it seemed as though water could be squeezed from it.","Ice-grade jadeite pendants, crystal-clear and translucent, glimmering with a faint green sheen.","Imperial-green jade cabochons, their rich color unmistakable evidence of their immense value.","There were also white jade ruyi ornaments, jadeite display pieces, Hetian jade necklaces...","The dazzling array filled the entire table, so brilliant it was almost dizzying to look at.","Zhang Yanyan casually picked up a white jade bangle and slipped it onto her wrist.","The cool, silky-smooth jade felt wonderfully comfortable against her skin.","There were plenty of gemstones in the spirit spring space, but none of them had been crafted into such exquisite jewelry.","These pieces were for her own use and collection. She absolutely would not use them to charge the space.","After carefully picking and choosing, she selected more than a dozen sets of high-end jade jewelry she particularly liked.","Bracelets, pendants, rings, earrings—everything was included.","She also picked out three white jade ornaments, which would look perfect in the living room on the second floor of her space.","Every one of these top-grade pieces was a rare treasure worth a fortune.","Zhang Yanyan did not even bother asking the price. She simply told the sales assistant to pack them up.","Manager Wang stood to the side, smiling so broadly that his heart was practically bursting with joy.","After choosing the top-tier jewelry for her private collection, she had Manager Wang bring out some jade jewelry made from more ordinary materials as well.","“Pack up these, these, and these... I’ll take them all.”","Manager Wang froze for a moment, secretly wondering why the Zhang heiress would want such ordinary merchandise.","But the customer was always right, and he did not dare ask questions. He immediately arranged for the staff to start packing.","The jade pieces Zhang Yanyan had just selected were placed in brocade boxes and then loaded into shopping bags.","They were piled on the floor like two small mountains, an astonishing quantity.","Zhang Yanyan gave them a cursory glance. Yes, that should be enough to keep the space running for quite some time.","She took the original owner’s black card from her bag and placed it on the coffee table.","“Run the card.”","The black card passed through the POS machine, and the payment went through instantly without the slightest hesitation.","The amount was so enormous that the sales assistants all drew in sharp breaths, while Manager Wang beamed with delight and personally directed the packing.","More than a dozen employees worked swiftly, sorting and packing all the merchandise.","They carefully carried everything out and loaded it into the Bentley’s trunk and two cargo vans.","The vehicles were packed to the brim, without even a sliver of empty space.","Manager Wang personally saw Zhang Yanyan to her car, bowing repeatedly as he thanked her.","“Take care, Miss Zhang. If you need anything in the future, just let us know! We’ll have everything prepared for you right away!”","Zhang Yanyan waved and had Uncle Li drive them to the next stop."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Gambling Stone Market","paragraphs":["The next stop was Rongcheng’s largest jade gambling market, where countless uncut jade stones were piled high.","Zhang Yanyan had come to try her luck. After all, money was the one thing she had plenty of now.","If she really couldn’t figure out the ins and outs of the trade, she could always buy stones that had already been cut open. That would lower the risk. Otherwise, if she spent a fortune on a pile of worthless rocks, she’d be completely screwed.","The moment her car drove into the market, the place exploded with noise.","Voices, hawkers’ shouts, haggling, and cries of surprise all blended into one deafening cacophony.","Raw stones of every size were piled into little hills, stretching so far that she couldn’t see the end of them.","As soon as she got out of the car, the stone-cutting area nearby caught her attention.","A cutting machine stood in the middle, surrounded by layer upon layer of spectators. It was even livelier than a marketplace.","With nothing better to do, Zhang Yanyan joined the crowd and stood at the outer edge to watch.","Standing in front of the cutting machine was a middle-aged man in a dark navy jacket. He was Boss Wang, a regular at the market. His face was tense as he gripped a moderately sized raw stone in his hands.","“Master, please cut it carefully. Just follow the line I drew!”","Boss Wang patted the stone and called out to the cutter, his voice trembling slightly.","The cutter was a seasoned hand in his fifties. With a cigarette dangling from his mouth, he nodded.","“Don’t worry, Old Wang. You still don’t trust my skills?”","The machine began to roar. The blade pressed into the stone, sending white stone dust spraying in every direction.","Everyone around held their breath, craning their necks forward and staring fixedly at the stone that was about to be opened.","“Look at that—green! It’s Imperial Green! And the water quality is excellent!”","The cutter was the first to shout. The crowd erupted in thunderous cheers.","Boss Wang lunged forward, clutching the newly opened stone. His hands were shaking.","“It really has green in it! I’ve finally hit the jackpot for once!”","A jeweler wearing a thick gold chain immediately pushed to the front and gestured with his hand.","“Brother Wang, I’ll take this piece. Three hundred thousand yuan! Cash or transfer, either works!”","A longtime customer who specialized in jade processing quickly chimed in from the side.","“Three hundred and ten thousand! Judging by the material, it should produce at least two bangles. I’ll pay three hundred and ten thousand!”","“Three hundred and twenty thousand! I’m short on this kind of material at my shop. Don’t fight me for it!”","“Three hundred and thirty thousand! Old Wang, we’ve worked together for so many years. Do me a favor!”","The bids came one after another, rising by ten or twenty thousand yuan at a time, while the onlookers shouted and egged them on.","Boss Wang grinned from ear to ear. He didn’t rush to accept any offer, simply letting them continue bidding.","“Three hundred and seventy thousand! That’s my final offer. Any higher and it won’t be worth it for me!”","The gold-chain jeweler gritted his teeth as he called out the price, then wiped the sweat from his forehead.","After two seconds of silence, a female owner of a high-end jewelry business spoke up.","“Three hundred and eighty thousand.”","No one else raised the bid.","After all, only a small opening had been cut, and there was still plenty of uncertainty inside. Three hundred and eighty thousand was already the highest reasonable price.","Boss Wang immediately made the decision.","“Sold! Three hundred and eighty thousand to Sister Li!”","The two of them scanned the payment code and completed the transfer on the spot, quick and efficient.","As soon as the money arrived, Boss Wang pulled a two-thousand-yuan red envelope from his wallet and stuffed it into the cutter’s hands.","“Master, let me share in your good luck. Thanks a lot! I’m buying drinks tonight!”","The stone-cutting master tucked the red envelope into his pocket, his eyes crinkling with a smile. “Thank you, Boss Wang! You’re far too generous. More importantly, you picked good rough stones—you’ve got a sharp eye and great luck.","“I only put in a bit of effort and happened to catch the right moment. I wish you smooth sailing ahead and profits overflowing your coffers!”","As Zhang Yanyan watched, Old Li, dressed in a gray shirt, squeezed through the crowd toward the stone-cutting machine with a large rock in his arms.","“Master, it’s my turn, it’s my turn! While the good luck from just now is still around, help me cut mine too!”","He rubbed his hands together, his face full of anticipation. Clearly, he had been waiting for a long time, hoping to ride this wave of good fortune.","Someone nearby teased him, “Old Li, that stone of yours doesn’t look very promising. Think it has a chance?”","Old Li waved dismissively. “Don’t talk nonsense. I picked this one out carefully. It’s definitely going to yield green!”","The stone-cutting master nodded, secured the rough stone, and switched on the machine.","The blade sliced through the rock with a piercing screech, sending stone dust flying everywhere.","Everyone watched intently. But the blade cut straight through, revealing a dull gray interior without even the faintest speck of green.","It was a worthless rock. The cut had been a bust.","Old Li’s face fell at once. He crouched on the ground, stroking the stone as he sighed in despair.","“It’s over, it’s over! I paid eighty-eight thousand for this, and it’s all gone down the drain! What rotten luck!”","Someone beside him tried to console him. “Old Li, that’s stone gambling for you—one cut can send you to heaven, the next to hell. Just accept the loss.”","Old Li slapped his thigh, his face full of regret. “I never should’ve gotten greedy. Now look at me—I’ve practically lost my entire savings!”","Honestly, stone gambling was exactly that: one cut could make you rich, another could leave you poor. Anything involving gambling was never a good thing.","Zhang Yanyan grumbled inwardly. This was worse than buying lottery tickets.","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍least lottery tickets cost only two yuan each. If you lost, you were only out two yuan—not enough to hurt.","But with rough stones, even a random piece could cost several thousand, or tens of thousands. If it turned out to be worthless, the pain was immediate. Plenty of people had even lost everything over it.","She wandered around the stone-cutting area, listening to the chatter around her and seeing more than enough scenes of joy and sorrow.","Some people splurged on rough stones, only to cut open one useless rock after another, their faces turning ashen.","Others casually picked out a small piece and ended up uncovering premium jade, making a fortune in one stroke.","“Do you think there’s any real method to this stone gambling business? To me, it all looks like luck.”","“What method could there be? It’s all guesswork. Nine out of ten gamblers lose—it’s just for the thrill.”","“Exactly. Just yesterday, someone lost several hundred thousand and burst into tears right on the spot.”","The onlookers gathered together and murmured among themselves, sharing the bitter realities of the stone-gambling trade.","In this business, everything depended on skill and luck. Without real expertise, no one should dare get involved lightly.","Zhang Yanyan rubbed her chin, making up her mind. If worse came to worst, she would just buy stones with the jade already exposed.","It wasn’t as though she lacked money. There was no need for her to take blind risks along with everyone else.","When Boss Liu, the owner of the stone-gambling yard, heard that the Zhang heiress had arrived, he immediately rushed out of his office.","He was a somewhat plump middle-aged man, his face covered in a shrewd yet polished smile.","He hurried over, his manner exceedingly respectful.","“Miss Zhang! Your presence in my humble little establishment truly brings it great honor!”","Boss Liu bent at the waist, his tone brimming with ingratiating warmth, terrified of giving offense to such an important patron.","Zhang Yanyan was not an ill-mannered person, so she smiled and replied,","“Boss Liu, you’re too kind. It’s my first time here, so I’m just looking around and broadening my horizons.”","Her tone was easygoing, without the slightest hint of a wealthy heiress’s arrogance.","Hearing this, Boss Liu smiled even more eagerly and quickly waved his hands.","“Please, take your time looking around and choose whatever you like. All the rough stones here are shipped directly from the old mines in Myanmar—completely genuine!”","“If you take a fancy to any of them, I’ll give you my absolute lowest price. I guarantee it’ll be thirty percent cheaper than elsewhere! We never overcharge our customers, so you can rest assured!”","He knew exactly how things stood. With the Zhang family’s power, he would be crazy not to curry favor with them.","Zhang Yanyan nodded and said with a smile, “Then I’ll trouble you, Boss Liu. I’ll look around on my own for now.”","With that, she headed toward the largest pile of rough stones.","Her bodyguards, A-Li and A-Hu, followed closely behind, never leaving her side.","Uncle Li, the driver, waited beside the truck, ready to load the stones at any moment.","Several nearby stall owners who had gathered to watch the spectacle huddled together and whispered among themselves.","“That’s the Zhang family’s eldest daughter? She looks so young, and she’s here to gamble on stones too?”","“She’s not short of money. She’s probably just here for fun. Unlike us—we depend on this to make a living.”","“Exactly. A wealthy heiress can make more from playing around with a few stones than we do in a whole year.”","Zhang Yanyan pretended not to hear them. She walked over to the largest pile of rough stones, crouched down, and put on an expression of curiosity.","She reached out and lightly ran her fingers over the rough, jagged stones, merely groping around at random.","After all, she knew nothing about this business. She had not even brought a flashlight for examining the stones.","The moment her fingertips touched a black-skinned rough stone, her mind suddenly gave a low buzz.","A surge of energy so rich it seemed almost ready to spill over shot through her palm and entered her soul.","The sensation was incredibly clear, like being jolted by electricity, and she froze on the spot."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Return with a Full Load","paragraphs":["Thinking it had been a hallucination, she reached over and touched another ordinary yellow-sandstone.","This time, there was no reaction at all. The stone was dead heavy, without the slightest trace of energy.","Zhang Yanyan frowned and picked up another rough stone marked with pine-flower patterns.","A faint ripple of energy drifted toward her, so weak that she could barely sense it.","Her heart gave a jolt, and she instantly understood what was happening. So that was it!","The Soul Refining Formula she cultivated had strengthened her spiritual soul, allowing her to sense the energy within jade!","Stones that produced no energy response were worthless pieces of waste rock.","The stronger the energy fluctuation, the better the quality of the jade inside.","This was practically a cheat code for the jade gambling world. It would be difficult for her to lose even if she wanted to!","Zhang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍Yanyan suppressed the excitement in her heart and pretended to be a complete novice who knew nothing.","She continued touching the rough stones at an unhurried pace, her movements casual enough to reveal nothing unusual.","She understood the principle of not flaunting one’s wealth. She couldn’t expose herself right from the start.","She selected the rough stones according to the energy fluctuations she sensed, while keeping her choices measured.","She picked out every stone with exceptionally strong energy, certain that they contained top-grade glass-jade.","As for the decent mid-grade jade, she only selected some of it instead of taking everything.","The low-grade bean-jade stones with barely any energy were ignored entirely.","She wasn’t short of that little bit of money anyway, so there was no need to waste her effort hauling away stones of little value.","More importantly, she couldn’t take all the good stones. Otherwise, she would ruin Boss Liu’s business.","He had treated her with courtesy, and there was no need for her to be so ruthless.","As long as she left plenty of jade-bearing stones behind—even if none of them were of the highest quality—the business could continue operating normally.","One should always leave room for others; there would be opportunities to meet again in the future. Zhang Yanyan understood that much.","Boss Liu watched her from not far away, his heart filled with doubt. He walked over and asked in a low voice, “Miss Zhang, don’t you need a flashlight to inspect the skin and pine-flower markings on the rough stones? We have professional tools here.”","Zhang Yanyan looked up and smiled. “No need, Boss Liu. This is my first time here, so I’m just looking around and broadening my horizons. I’ll choose whatever catches my eye. Maybe I’ll get lucky.”","Boss Liu suddenly understood and nodded with a smile. “Exactly, exactly! You’re just here to have fun. Do whatever feels comfortable!”","He didn’t dare ask any more questions or disturb her. He simply stood to the side with a smile on his face, waiting attentively.","Nearby, a worker whispered, “This young lady is way too casual when picking stones. She only touches them a couple of times before setting them aside. Isn’t she afraid of losing money?”","“She’s rich. Losing a few hundred thousand yuan is probably just a game to her. There’s no need for us to worry.”","Zhang Yanyan squatted there for nearly half an hour and gradually selected more than thirty stones.","They varied in size. All of them were top quality, though there were also some decent glutinous- and ice-jade stones among them, of which she took only a small number.","The stones filled exactly two trucks—neither too many nor too few. It was just right.","She stood up, brushed the dust and stone chips from her hands, and let out a breath.","“Boss Liu, that’s everything. Please arrange for your workers to load them onto the trucks. There’s no need to open them here. Just take them away directly.”","She didn’t dare have them opened here. Every single one would yield jade, and people would surely think she was some kind of monster.","Boss Liu immediately agreed and shouted, “Everyone, get over here! Move quickly and load Miss Zhang’s rough stones onto the trucks. Handle them carefully—don’t damage anything!”","Several workers rushed over at once. Some lifted while others carried. The rough stones were heavy enough that even the workers struggled with them.","Before long, both trucks were packed full, with everything stacked neatly and securely.","Zhang Yanyan walked over and paid by card. After calculating the total, Boss Liu even gave her a twenty-percent discount.","He thanked her repeatedly and clasped his fist as he said, “Thank you for supporting my business, Miss Zhang! Come again next time, and I’ll save the best new material for you!”","Zhang Yanyan smiled. “You’re too kind. I’ll come back whenever I need anything.”","With that, she got into the Bentley with her accompanying bodyguards. The two trucks loaded with rough stones followed behind as they slowly drove away from the jade gambling yard.","Leaning against the soft seat, Zhang Yanyan couldn’t help letting the corners of her lips curl upward.","She had gained so much from this trip. She had made a killing!","She now had top-grade jewelry, jade for charging the space, and enough high-quality rough stones stocked up.","With this cheat ability, obtaining jade and gemstones in the future would be as easy as reaching into her pocket.","All she wanted now was to hurry back to the estate and take a good look at her treasures.","By the time Zhang Yanyan and the others arrived at the Zhang family estate’s villa district, it was already afternoon.","Uncle Chen had long since brought the security team and servants to wait at the entrance.","When he saw the two trucks loaded with rough stones following behind the Bentley, a trace of surprise flashed through his eyes. However, he strictly adhered to his duties and didn’t ask a single unnecessary question. Bowing respectfully, he said, “Miss, you must be tired. Shall we put these rough stones in the underground vault first?”","The Zhang family’s underground vault had tight security, with surveillance covering every corner and maximum protection in place. It was extremely safe.","Zhang Yanyan nodded. “Yes. Move everything inside, and be careful. Don’t damage anything.”","Uncle Chen immediately took out his phone and began arranging personnel. In a short while, professional movers and equipment had all been brought in.","The workers first transferred the rough stones from the trucks into specialized storage crates, securing and stacking them properly. They then used a small electric forklift to transport them.","The compact forklift was both flexible and stable. It lifted the heavy crates of stones securely and carried them straight to the underground vault along the planned route. The entire process was efficient and precise, with no risk of the stones slipping or being damaged.","Uncle Chen directed everything from the side, overseeing every stage of the transport to ensure that nothing went wrong.","Before long, the enormous underground vault was packed to the brim.","Uncle Chen arranged for guards to remain on duty, then quietly led the servants out and thoughtfully closed the door behind them.","The vault instantly fell silent. It was so quiet that Zhang Yanyan could hear her own heartbeat.","She glanced around, shut off all the surveillance cameras, and confirmed that there was no one else present.","With a gentle movement of her thoughts, the piles of rough stones and jade vanished without a trace.","She had stored everything inside the Yunhua Space without the slightest effort.","She placed the jewelry she had bought and liked directly in the dressing room on the second floor of the space.","There, she arranged it neatly alongside the jewelry left behind by the original owner.","She put the highest-quality jade rough stones directly into the stationary zone.","As for the ordinary jade jewelry and rough stones, she tossed them all into the spiritual spring inside the space.","The moment the spring water touched the jade, a faint green radiance immediately rippled across its surface.","The jade melted at a speed visible to the naked eye, transforming into pure energy.","The energy continuously poured into the core of the space, nourishing the entire Yunhua Space.","The next second, a thunderous boom suddenly rang out inside the space.","White mist surged wildly, and the entire space began to tremble violently.","Zhang Yanyan felt her mind shake. She hurriedly steadied herself and didn’t dare move recklessly.","Once the trembling finally stopped, she quickly entered the Yunhua Space with a thought.","The scene before her filled her with both shock and delight. She nearly jumped for joy on the spot.","The entire space had actually doubled in size. Its area had expanded to twice what it had been!","The self-built house remained as it was, standing steadily in the very center of the space.","The Yunhua Supermarket on the first floor was still brightly lit, with all its goods arranged in neat rows.","The courtyard, storage shed, and side rooms had all expanded as well, becoming considerably more spacious.","What delighted her most was the farmland in the backyard.","It had originally been only three mu, but now it had doubled to six.","The soil was dark and rich, even more fertile than before, releasing the fresh fragrance of earth.","The fish pond had doubled in size as well. Sunlight shimmered across its surface, and the water was so clear that the bottom could be seen.","The number of fish fry it could support had doubled too. From now on, she would never have to worry about running out of fish.","The woodland behind the hill had expanded by a large stretch, lush and green, rolling into the distance.","With so much more land available, they could plant many more fruit trees and raise more livestock and poultry.","Zhang Yanyan squatted on the ridge between the fields, looking at everything before her with a helpless smile."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Capacity Expansion","paragraphs":["Expanding the space was a wonderful thing, but it was also incredibly exhausting.","Only yesterday, she had painstakingly turned over the soil, sown seeds, and planted fruit saplings.","Now that the space had expanded, all the newly revealed land was barren. She would have to spend another half a day working on it.","The seedlings she had planted earlier were all clustered on one side, while a vast stretch of empty land lay beside them.","Supporting her aching lower back, she let out a helpless sigh.","This surprise had come far too suddenly, leaving her completely unprepared.","She was genuinely exhausted, but genuinely happy too—a perfect case of suffering and joy at the same time.","Fortunately, she had received a complete set of smart, fully automatic agricultural machinery from today’s sign-in reward.","With a thought, she took the entire set of machines out of the space.","There was a tiller, a seeder, a watering machine, a harvester—in short, everything she could possibly need.","She pressed the start button, and the machines began operating automatically with a steady hum.","The newly expanded fields beside her were turned into neat, orderly rows. The soil was even smoother and finer than anything she could have managed by hand.","This was great!","With these machines, most of her workload would be taken care of.","She would never again have to exhaust herself plowing the land manually. It was practically a blessing for lazy people.","Zhang Yanyan took out the seeds left over from yesterday and began sowing them in separate sections.","Three mu of land were dedicated to vegetables: bok choy, Chinese cabbage, cucumbers, tomatoes, chili peppers, and more.","The crops were planted in neat rows with even spacing. Just looking at them was satisfying.","Another three mu were reserved for grain crops: rice, wheat, corn, and soybeans.","With the space’s tenfold time acceleration, the seeds would sprout and grow into seedlings in just a few days.","Once the seeds had been sown, the watering machine automatically began spraying them with water from the fishpond, enhanced with a small amount of spirit spring water.","Nourished by the spirit spring water, the seeds would germinate faster and grow more vigorously.","After tidying up the fields, Zhang Yanyan turned her attention to the expanded fishpond and the rear mountain.","The fish fry and young livestock and poultry she had bought yesterday were nowhere near enough to fill the new areas.","She would also need to buy more fruit saplings. Otherwise, leaving the rear mountain empty would be a waste.","She rubbed her aching shoulders, panting from exhaustion. Her back and waist were sore all over.","The expanded space would keep her busy for several days.","Still, when she imagined the future harvest, she felt as though she had regained all her energy.","She walked over to the spirit spring, crouched down, and cupped a handful of water to drink.","The sweet, clear spring water slid down her throat, and a warm current instantly spread throughout her body.","Most of her fatigue vanished. Her entire body felt relaxed, and her strength returned as well.","The spirit spring really was a top-tier treasure. One drink when she was tired, and she was immediately revived at full strength.","Looking at the vast, empty new areas in the space, Zhang Yanyan’s heart filled with anticipation.","Tomorrow, she would definitely go on a major shopping trip to the agricultural supply market and the livestock and poultry market.","She would buy more fruit saplings, fish fry, and young livestock and poultry, filling every available space.","Once the fruit trees covered the rear mountain, the fish fry filled the pond, and the livestock and poultry occupied the foot of the mountain, the entire place would soon be overflowing with fragrant fruits under the tenfold growth rate.","Before long, there would be more vegetables than she could eat and mountains of grain. She would never have to worry about food again.","The fishpond would be full of plump fish and prawns, while chickens and ducks would flock across the rear mountain, with cattle and sheep roaming everywhere.","With such a treasure of a space, she could live comfortably for the rest of her life.","As for the male lead in the novel, Song Ze, and the white lotus, Tang Tang, she could not be bothered to spare them even a glance.","She had no desire whatsoever to get involved with them and would avoid them at all costs.","She would never allow the original host’s tragic fate to repeat itself.","Love and hatred, family feuds among wealthy clans—all of it had nothing to do with her.","Zhang Yanyan withdrew her consciousness from the space and opened the door to the vault.","Outside, dusk had already settled in. The setting sun had dyed the estate a warm golden color.","Auntie Chen had prepared an entire table of delicious dishes and was waiting for her in the living room.","There was braised fish, sweet-and-sour ribs, stir-fried lettuce stems, and mushroom soup.","They were all her favorite home-cooked dishes, steaming hot and fragrant.","The aroma drifted over, and Zhang Yanyan’s stomach immediately began to growl.","After washing her hands, she sat down at the dining table, her appetite instantly awakened.","Auntie Chen sat beside her and kept piling food onto her plate, her eyes full of affection.","“Miss, you must be exhausted today. Eat some more. This braised fish was just made. It’ll help restore your energy.”","Zhang Yanyan’s mouth was stuffed full, so she answered indistinctly.","“Auntie Chen, your cooking is the best! I could eat three whole bowls of rice!”","The hot food warmed her from the inside out, and happiness flooded her heart.","After working hard all day, being able to enjoy such a comforting meal was incredibly satisfying.","She ate in great gulps, leaving all the day’s fatigue behind.","Seeing how heartily she was eating, Auntie Chen’s smile grew even gentler.","“Slow down, sweetheart. Don’t choke. The soup is still hot—have another two bowls.”","“You’ve been out all day, so you must be starving. If it’s not enough, I’ll fry another dish for you.”","Zhang Yanyan waved her hand. “No need, Auntie Chen. This is plenty. It’s delicious!”","After dinner, Zhang Yanyan returned to the bedroom on the second floor.","She was too tired to practice the Spirit Refining Art again. After such a long day, she needed a good rest.","Lying on the bed, she took out her phone and began browsing information about the agricultural supply market.","She already had a clear plan for tomorrow’s shopping trip.","She would buy dozens more fruit saplings and plant them all over the expanded rear mountain.","She would double the amount of fish fry, adding carp, grass carp, crucian carp, prawns, crabs, and more.","She would also increase the number of young livestock and poultry—chickens, ducks, geese, cattle, sheep, pigs, and anything else she could find.","She would fill the breeding area at the foot of the mountain until it was packed and lively.","Zhang Yanyan woke up and stretched luxuriously.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍looked at the bright sunlight outside the window and called out to the system in her mind, “Eighteen, today’s sign-in.”","The next second, Eighteen’s mechanical prompt sounded in her mind right on schedule.","[Sign-in successful! Congratulations, Host. You have received today’s daily sign-in rewards—]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a purple-tier reward: One Intelligent Agricultural Management Hub for the Entire Space. Once bound to the space, it can automatically manage the entire process of cultivation, irrigation, fertilization, harvesting, and animal husbandry. It is perfectly compatible with the space’s tenfold time acceleration and allows customized planting and breeding plans, freeing your hands from all manual operations.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a blue-tier reward: One Customized Four-Wheel-Drive Off-Road RV. It comes equipped with an independent kitchen and bathroom, a constant-temperature energy storage system, smart devices throughout the vehicle, and an oversized sealed storage compartment. Its registration and licensing have already been completed, and it can be retrieved for use at any time!]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a blue-tier reward: One Complete Seed and Seedling Gift Pack of Rare, High-Yield Varieties. It includes vegetables, grain and oil crops, fruit trees, and rare medicinal herbs. All varieties have a 100% germination rate, are suited to the space’s soil and water conditions, and can be planted directly.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a green-tier reward: One Complete Set of Top-Tier Professional Gaming Equipment. It includes a customized high-performance computer, an ultra-high-definition monitor, an ergonomic controller, and immersive noise-canceling headphones. Its performance is maxed out and compatible with all kinds of games.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a green-tier reward: One Customized Ladies’ Mechanical Wristwatch. It has a simple, versatile casual design, is waterproof and scratch-resistant, and is suitable for daily commutes and outings.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a green-tier reward: One Full-Body Smart Massage Chair. It supports multiple professional massage modes, deeply relieves muscle soreness, soothes fatigue, and allows its position to be adjusted with a single button.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a white-tier reward: Three Sets of Waterproof, Stain-Resistant, Wear-Resistant Protective Work Clothes. They are breathable without feeling stuffy and are suitable for farm work, transporting supplies, and other tasks.]","[Congratulations, Host, on receiving a white-tier reward: Ten Pairs of Thickened, Non-Slip, Wear-Resistant Protective Work Gloves. They are puncture-resistant and waterproof, and are suitable for cultivation, transporting supplies, and a variety of other situations.]","【Congratulations, Host, on obtaining a white-tier reward: ×4 Home HD Night-Vision Security Camera Sets. They can be remotely controlled via smartphone, are waterproof and dustproof, and provide all-around protection for the safety of the estate.】","【Congratulations, Host, on obtaining a white-tier reward: ×6 Complete Sets of Blackout, Thickened, Soundproof Curtains. They provide heat and sound insulation, are suitable for bedrooms and studies, and greatly improve sleep quality.】","【Congratulations, Host, on obtaining a white-tier reward: ×4 Sets of Pure Cotton, Skin-Friendly All-Season Loungewear. Soft, breathable, and comfortable for relaxing at home.】","【All rewards have been stored in the system space. The Host may withdraw them freely at any time.】","Zhang Yanyan’s eyes lit up at once, and her thoughts instantly swept through the system space.","The silver-gray off-road motorhome was parked steadily in an empty area of the space. Every detail of its interior was clearly visible, and its features were even more impressive than those of several mass-produced models she had looked at before. Its oversized storage compartment was just the right size to hold the seedlings and supplies she would be purchasing later.","What delighted her most was the intelligent control hub for the space. With it, whenever the space expanded in the future, she would only need to tap a few buttons on the hub, completely freeing her hands from the work.","The remaining rewards were all incredibly practical as well, perfectly suited to her current needs. She casually arranged the various items in their designated storage areas within the space, leaving the motorhome and the agricultural management hub where they were for the time being, her heart brimming with satisfaction.","She rolled out of bed and shuffled into the bathroom in her slippers.","After washing her face with warm water, she was completely awake. She changed into a loose black casual outfit, paired it with a versatile pair of white sneakers, casually tied her hair into a high ponytail, and went downstairs bare-faced.","In the dining room, Auntie Chen had already set out breakfast. There were freshly steamed pork buns, millet porridge simmered until smooth and creamy, boiled eggs, and a dish of crisp pickled radish—all simple, homestyle foods with flavors that were easy to enjoy."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Progress","paragraphs":["Just as Zhang Yanyan sat down and picked up her chopsticks, the butler, Uncle Chen, hurried over. He held himself ramrod straight, his manner respectful.","“Miss, I’d like to update you on the villa renovations.”","Uncle Chen bowed slightly, his posture deferential. “The whole-house smart system and top-of-the-line security system have all been inspected and fully tested. They’ve also been linked with the estate’s security team for round-the-clock coordination.","“The full-wall bookcases in the study and the equipment in the gaming area are all in place.","“The bedding and toiletries in the master bedroom and guest rooms have been stocked according to the brands and styles you specified.","“The interior furnishings are currently about eighty percent complete. The remaining artwork, greenery, and decorative pieces will all be finished tomorrow. After one day of ventilation, the villa will be ready for you to move in with just your luggage the day before school starts.","“The cleaning, security, and housekeeping teams for the villa have also been screened in advance and can start work at any time.”","Zhang Yanyan took a bite of her bun. Only after chewing and swallowing did she reply, “Got it. There’s no need to report the progress to me every day from now on. Once everything is completely finished, just let me know that I can move in.","“There are still several days before school starts, so we should have enough time. There’s no need to rush—just make sure every detail is handled properly.”","“Yes, Miss. You can rest assured.” Uncle Chen bowed in acknowledgment. He said nothing more and quietly stepped aside.","Zhang ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Yanyan finished her breakfast at a leisurely pace, wiped her mouth, picked up the car keys from the cabinet in the foyer, and headed outside.","She didn’t drive her previous car. Instead, she chose a low-key black SUV. Since she was going to the market today, she drove herself and didn’t bring along a bodyguard or chauffeur. It would be more convenient to shop on her own.","The engine started, and the car glided out of the estate, heading straight for the large agricultural and livestock market on the outskirts of the city.","After the space had expanded yesterday, the farmland, forests, and fishponds had all doubled in size. The seedlings and young animals she had bought earlier were nowhere near enough to fill them. Her top priority today was to make up the shortfall.","After parking at the market, Zhang Yanyan didn’t rush to browse the shops. She went to the market’s administration office first.","She had a wide variety of goods to buy, and in large quantities at that. She didn’t want to waste time hauling everything back and forth, so renting a temporary storage warehouse for staging was the safest option.","“Hello, I’d like to rent a temporary warehouse with a loading and unloading area. I’ll only need it for one day, and I’d prefer something fairly spacious with good security.”","She got straight to the point, and the staff quickly processed the paperwork. They assigned her a transfer warehouse located toward the inner section of the market. Its exterior perimeter was covered by cameras with no blind spots, while there were no cameras inside. After paying the rent and receiving the key, Zhang Yanyan turned and entered the market.","Her first stop was the agricultural supplies and seed market. People streamed through the aisles, while neat, branded agricultural supply shops lined both sides. The dry scent of seeds and soil hung in the air.","Zhang Yanyan went straight to the largest shop she had visited last time. The owner, Boss Wang, was standing at the entrance, counting a shipment of newly arrived goods. When he looked up and saw her, he immediately greeted her with a smile.","“Hey, it’s you again! Did you plant the seeds you bought last time? How was the germination rate?”","Boss Wang spoke to her like an old acquaintance. Zhang Yanyan had purchased a huge batch of seeds from him before, leaving a deep impression. He simply assumed she was a customer who owned a large farm and had no idea about her family background.","“Pretty good. The germination rate was very high, so I’ve come back to restock.” Zhang Yanyan walked into the shop, her gaze sweeping over the seed packets lining the shelves.","“Do you have any newly released vegetable varieties that taste good and are highly disease-resistant? And could you recommend some rare grains I haven’t bought before, along with food crops that are suitable for dense planting and have stable yields?”","“You’ve come to the right person!” Boss Wang immediately perked up and led her over to the shelves, introducing the products one by one.","“Take this cucumber, for example. It’s a new variety—crisp, sweet, and seedless, with especially strong disease resistance. It doesn’t need a complicated trellis, and it’ll even produce well in a pot.","“And this tomato has a sandy, meaty texture. It’s an improved version of an old variety, with plenty of juice and a sweet-and-tangy flavor. It tastes far better than the ordinary varieties on the market.","“For grains, we have black wheat, quinoa, chickpeas, and highland barley. They’re all new varieties this year, with stable yields and high nutritional value.","“For food crops, I recommend this short-stalked waxy corn. It has a high rate of producing two ears per plant, doesn’t attract many pests, and has a wonderfully chewy texture. It’s our best seller.”","Zhang Yanyan listened attentively, occasionally asking a question or two. “How much can this cucumber produce per acre? Does the tomato have high sunlight requirements? And roughly how long is the growing cycle for these grains?”","Boss Wang answered every question clearly and thoroughly, without the slightest hesitation.","Once she had all the details, Zhang Yanyan placed her order right away. “For each of the vegetable varieties you just mentioned, give me ten packets. For the grains, fifteen packets of each. I’ll also take twenty packets each of the high-yield varieties of rice, wheat, and corn. And for any herb and spice seeds you carry, give me two packets of each.”","Boss Wang’s eyes lit up. He hurriedly agreed. “Sure thing, sure thing! I’ll pack everything up right now! Since you’re buying so much, I’ll give you fifteen percent off. I’ll also throw in ten bags of seedling mix and two bags of special organic fertilizer. I guarantee everything you plant will grow vigorously!”","“Sounds good. Thank you.” Zhang Yanyan nodded.","After Boss Wang had packed and sealed all the seeds into boxes, she left him the address of the warehouse she had just rented and her contact information. She paid the bill and asked him to arrange for a truck to deliver everything there before noon that day. Then she turned and headed for the livestock market next door.","The livestock market was considerably livelier than the agricultural supply market. Licensed breeding shops stood in neat rows along the passageways, while the calls of livestock and poultry rose and fell without pause. The air carried the distinctive scent of a farming facility.","Zhang Yanyan went to the reputable breeding shop with the most complete credentials in the market. The owner, Boss Li, was introducing some young animals to a customer. The moment he saw her enter, he immediately greeted her with a smile.","“Miss, what kind of young animals are you looking for? Everything we sell comes from licensed breeding operations, and all the vaccinations are up to date. Their survival rate is guaranteed!”","Zhang Yanyan glanced over the animal cages and asked, “I bought a batch from you before. I’ve expanded my facilities, so I’d like to add a few more. Could you recommend some breeds for me? What kind of chickens have both a high egg-laying rate and good-quality meat?","“As for ducks, which breeds taste good, grow quickly, and aren’t prone to illness? And what breeds of cattle and sheep are suitable for confined raising—good breeds with steady growth?”","Boss Li immediately began introducing them one by one. “For chickens, I’d strongly recommend the barred chicken and the green-shelled layer. Barred chickens have firm, flavorful meat, grow quickly, and lay steadily. Green-shelled layers produce eggs with high nutritional value that also command a higher price. Both breeds are easy to raise and highly disease-resistant.","“For ducks, go with the Beijing duck. It grows quickly, tolerates rough feed, and can be ready for market in three months. It’s good for both meat and eggs.","“For cattle, Simmental calves are your best choice. They grow quickly, have a high dressing percentage, and do perfectly well in confined housing.","“For sheep, I’d recommend Small-tailed Han sheep. They have a high twinning rate and can give birth twice a year, making them especially suitable for large-scale farming.”","Zhang Yanyan pressed him further. “How many vaccine shots have all these young animals received? Is there any after-sales guarantee? And for the cattle and sheep, will you include breeding males?”","“Don’t worry! Before any of the young animals leave here, they’ve all received two basic vaccinations and been dewormed. I guarantee a survival rate of over ninety percent. If any of them die from non-human causes within a week, I’ll replace them immediately! As for the cattle and sheep, I’ve already included suitable breeding males. It absolutely won’t affect their ability to reproduce!” Boss Li thumped his chest as he gave his assurance.","Now that Zhang Yanyan had a clear idea of things, she gave him the quantities directly. “Three hundred each of the barred Plymouth Rocks and green-egg-laying hens; two hundred Muscovy ducks; one hundred lion-head geese; fifteen Simmental calves; forty Small-Tailed Han lambs; twenty Tibetan pork piglets; fifty meat rabbits and fifty lop-eared rabbits; and one hundred and fifty pairs each of homing pigeons and meat pigeons.”"]}]);
